pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBasicDreamControl a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Basic dream control"@en, "Grundlegende Traumsteuerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choose a theme (a subject, place or person). First way: before sleep do a relaxation exercise, state clearly what one wills to dream (for example of one's father) and let the mind drift into sleep. Second way: hold a scene or image lightly in attention while falling asleep. Third way: use a sigil, drawn or chanted (Chapter Five)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 74; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWillingDreamContent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Willing dream content"@en, "Trauminhalt willentlich bestimmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intentionally guiding the content of one's dreams."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 74; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDreamControlMethodsGuideDreamsYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dream control methods guide dreams"@en, "Traumsteuerungsmethoden lenken Träume"@de ;
    skos:definition "The three approaches are offered as ways of intentionally guiding dream content."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBasicDreamControl ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWillingDreamContent ;
