pmc:ChaosMagicCondBLucidityTriggers a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lucidity and its triggers"@en, "Luzidität und ihre Auslöser"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lucidity is realising one is dreaming so the dream can be changed; it may be triggered by an incongruity (Hine noticed shoes he did not own in an otherwise perfect dream) or by recognising a recurring dream one does not want to repeat."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBExtendedLucidDreaming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Extended lucid dreaming"@en, "Ausgedehntes luzides Träumen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Extending flashes of lucidity so as to direct dream content for magical purposes."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"possible\")."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBInducingLucidityTriggerMetaprogramming a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Inducing lucidity by trigger metaprogramming"@en, "Luzidität durch Auslöser-Metaprogrammierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use waking suggestion, or program yourself so that a specific dream image triggers lucidity (e.g. resolve to become lucid whenever a yellow sphere floats towards you); the sphere can be sent by another person or be a servitor designed for this."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBMetaprogrammingYieldsLucidityYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Metaprogramming yields lucidity"@en, "Metaprogrammierung ergibt Luzidität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Suggestion or a programmed trigger image brings about lucidity."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBInducingLucidityTriggerMetaprogramming ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBExtendedLucidDreaming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBNonWesternDreaming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-Western dreaming; Senoi"@en, "Nichtwestliches Träumen; Senoi"@de ;
    skos:definition "Approaching dreams from Aboriginal or Senoi views can be rewarding; some anthropologists credit Senoi dream psychology for their tranquil lives, reporting no violent crime or conflict for two to three centuries when first contacted in the 1930s."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 76; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAxisMundi a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Axis Mundi"@en, "Axis Mundi"@de ;
    skos:definition "The central axis joining every zone of experience and every state of consciousness, pictured as a World Tree, a Sacred Mountain, a pole or a Crossroads; less a location than a way of placing oneself, since being relaxed in the present sets one at the middle of one's magical reality; also the gateway to the innerworlds."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCentering a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Centering"@en, "Zentrierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Anything from a full banishing to a brief moment of relaxed no-mind. The core: 1) attend to one's bodily presence; 2) set up the gates, quarters or dimensions, in whatever scheme one uses, around oneself as centre; 3) identify with whatever one has chosen as a source of inspiration, joining macrocosm and microcosm. Gather several such exercises for different occasions, from banishings before heavy ritual to quick ones usable anywhere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBeingCentredPoised a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being centred and poised"@en, "Zentriert und handlungsbereit sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being relaxed, prepared and poised for action at the centre of one's magical reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRelaxedPreparedPoisedSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxed, prepared, poised"@en, "Entspannt, vorbereitet, bereit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A centring exercise is meant to leave one relaxed, ready and poised to act."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: after a centring exercise one feels relaxed, ready and poised to act. Stated as what the exercises ought to give; no deadline or rate."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCentering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCenteringYieldsPoiseYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Centering yields poise"@en, "Zentrierung ergibt Bereitschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Centering produces relaxation and readiness for action."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCentering ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBeingCentredPoised ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBTreeLifeShamanicWorldTree a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tree of Life from shamanic world-tree"@en, "Lebensbaum aus schamanischem Weltenbaum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine finds it a fair assumption that the Tree of Life of the Qabalah grew out of a shamanic tree of the world; the crossroads is named as a further axis symbol in Celtic, Greek and Haitian myth."@en ;
    skos:note "Put in the text as a reasonable assumption."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBInhabitantsInnerworldsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Inhabitants of the innerworlds"@en, "Bewohner der Innenwelten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The innerworlds are said to be crowded with spirits, demons and ancestors, with whom in a tribal society the shaman mediates contact for all."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "spirits, demons and ancestors" ;
    pm:nameRole "innerworld populations" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDeepMindReceptiveSuggestion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deep Mind receptive to suggestion"@en, "Tiefengeist empfänglich für Suggestion"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Deep Mind is said to take suggestion readily and to dress itself in any images, so that in the West a great range of innerworlds lies open."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 77; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBExploringAnyInnerworld a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exploring any innerworld"@en, "Beliebige Innenwelt erkunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "With the astral temple and the techniques for forming the Double, explore whatever magical innerworld one likes, from the mythic country of the Norse gods to gardens reached through the I Ching trigrams."@en ;
    skos:note "Presented as building on building an astral temple (pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBuildingAstralTemple), kinesthetic memory: raising the double's arm (pmp:ChaosMagicCondBKinestheticMemory)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBExploringAnyInnerworldYieldsInnerworldYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Exploring any innerworld yields innerworld exploration"@en, "Beliebige Innenwelt erkunden ergibt Erkundung der Innenwelten"@de ;
    skos:definition "With the astral temple and the body-formation techniques one is said to be able to explore any magical innerworld."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBExploringAnyInnerworld ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBInnerworldExploration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBInnerworldExploration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Innerworld exploration"@en, "Erkundung der Innenwelten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to enter and explore mythic innerworlds of any system."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBMagicalWillVectorIntentionality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical Will as vector of intentionality"@en, "Magischer Wille als Vektor der Intentionalität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Will is intention directed along a line; saying that one wills something casts it into the future; Magical Will is not willpower or concentration, and rests on relaxation in the present together with unity of desire and of purpose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBOathsStringentTestsFailFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Oaths and stringent tests fail"@en, "Eide und strenge Prüfungen scheitern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Setting stringent tests, oaths or promises is useless: if the wish to overcome a habit is weaker than the wish to keep it, you will surely fail and reinforce your sense of weakness."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: where the wish to overcome a habit is weaker than the wish to keep it, oaths, promises and stringent tests surely fail and confirm the sense of being weak. No deadline or rate; the failure is put on the operator's divided desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBIsolateDesireYetStayDetachedPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Isolate desire yet stay detached"@en, "Begehren isolieren und doch losgelöst bleiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Proficiency at sorcery requires being able to isolate, identify and focus on specific desires while becoming detached from them."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRefinedMagicalWill ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSorcery ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDesireManifestsOnceForgotten a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Desire manifests once forgotten"@en, "Begehren verwirklicht sich, wenn vergessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Desires are said to come about once they have been singled out, put outside oneself and then forgotten."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBUnityPurpose a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity of purpose"@en, "Einheit des Zwecks"@de ;
    skos:definition "Orchestrating perception and action along one directional vector, a relaxed single-mindedness detached from results; ritual acts serve as exercises in it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRitualProjectionTrainsUnityPurposeYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual projection trains unity of purpose"@en, "Ritualprojektion übt Einheit des Zwecks"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ritual acts are said to train unity of purpose."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBProjectingIntentSigilGestureCry ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBUnityPurpose ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBProjectingIntentSigilGestureCry a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Projecting intent with sigil, gesture and cry"@en, "Absicht projizieren mit Sigille, Geste und Schrei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualise the sigil of your desire; push the hand slowly forward as if against air resistance while visualising a beam of energy leaping from it; exhale with the cry 'Kia!', uniting thought, word and deed in a single projection into the future."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBImmovableWisdom a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Immovable Wisdom (Zen)"@en, "Unbewegliche Weisheit (Zen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doing one's Will requires relaxed single-mindedness while detached from intended results, likened to the Zen idea of a mind freed from attachments, past bonds and anticipation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWillNeedsPatienceVigilanceCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Will needs patience and vigilance"@en, "Wille braucht Geduld und Wachsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "This detachment does not come easily and needs much patience, discipline and practice; refining Will requires constant vigilance against slipping into habituated thought and behaviour."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRefinedMagicalWill ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRefinedMagicalWill a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Refined Magical Will"@en, "Verfeinerter magischer Wille"@de ;
    skos:definition "A refined Will: relaxed single-minded intention free of attachments."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBZenMeditationMartialArts a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Zen meditation and martial arts"@en, "Zen-Meditation und Kampfkünste"@de ;
    skos:definition "Simple meditation as in Zen, and martial arts practice, as supports for magical development."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 78; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBMeditationMartialArtsDevelopMagicalYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation and martial arts develop magical abilities"@en, "Meditation und Kampfkunst entwickeln magische Fähigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Simple meditation helps develop bodymind awareness, relaxation and present awareness; martial arts are called invaluable for developing magical abilities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBZenMeditationMartialArts ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWidenedBodyAwareness, pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRelaxationSkill, pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRefinedMagicalWill ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 4 Another Crack in the Wall, p. 79; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .


#
# Chapter Five, Playing with Chaos
#

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSorcery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sorcery"@en, "Zauberei (Sorcery)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sorcery is the use of magical methods and outlooks to change one's material surroundings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAgainstHighLowMagicSplit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the High/Low magic split"@en, "Gegen die Trennung von hoher und niederer Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine rejects the traditional distinction of 'Low' results magic and 'High' spiritual magic as perpetuating a matter/spirit split; chaos magic holds it artificial and a sign of self-limitation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFiveValuesSorcery a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five values of sorcery"@en, "Fünf Werte der Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sorcery is valued in chaos magic for five reasons: 1) success with it makes one certain that magic works; 2) examining one's motives and desire-complexes is itself illuminating; 3) it raises questions of ethics and of answering for the changes made; 4) it requires results one can point to; 5) it makes one attend to the world as it actually is."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCertaintyThatMagicWorks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Certainty that magic works"@en, "Gewissheit, dass Magie wirkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Embedded conviction that magic works, which success in sorcery gives in a way argument or aimless practice cannot."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSelfInsightThroughAnalysingDesire a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-insight through analysing desire"@en, "Selbsterkenntnis durch Begehrensanalyse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rigorous analysis of one's motivations and desire-complexes in sorcery is itself enlightening."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBResponsibilityPersonalChangeSorcery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Responsibility and personal change in sorcery"@en, "Verantwortung und persönlicher Wandel in der Zauberei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Serious sorcery entails accepting responsibility for changes caused, and bringing change tends to change oneself (enchanting for fame requires being able to change to use fame well); results must be identifiable (one must be able to say how sorcery contributed to wealth)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRetreatIntoSafeFantasyCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Retreat into safe fantasy"@en, "Rückzug in sichere Fantasie"@de ;
    skos:definition "A major hazard in magical growth is retreating into a comfortable fantasy when things become hard; sorcery, being about everyday life, is said to keep one grounded."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSorcery ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 80; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicCoreChaosTechnique a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil magic as core chaos technique"@en, "Sigillenmagie als Kerntechnik des Chaos"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sigil magic, derived from Austin Osman Spare, is simple, results-oriented and said to be effective regardless of belief; after the basics one may develop personal forms of sigil magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSpareAgainstPropsSystemLearning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spare against props and system-learning"@en, "Spare gegen Requisiten und Systemgelehrsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many of Spare's contemporaries thought magic impossible without robes, weapons, banners, an altar and command of systems like Qabalah; Spare's sigils showed that working magic could be done instantly and nearly anywhere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSigilProcessYieldsResultsMagicYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil process yields results magic"@en, "Sigillenprozess ergibt Ergebnismagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sigilisation is called among the plainest and most effective kinds of results magic."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBResultsMagicSigil ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSPLIFF a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "S.P.L.I.F.F. sigil process"@en, "S.P.L.I.F.F.-Sigillenprozess"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's six-stage acronym for sigil magic: Statement of Intent; Pathways available?; Link intent to symbolic carrier; Intense Gnosis/Indifferent Vacuity; Fire; Forget."@en ;
    skos:note "The text layer misreads the acronym, with an L for the I."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil magic (full process)"@en, "Sigillenmagie (Gesamtprozess)"@de ;
    skos:definition "1) Formulate a clear statement of intent; 2) check pathways for it to manifest; 3) turn the intent into a symbolic carrier (monogram, mantra, other media); 4) enter gnosis or indifferent vacuity; 5) fire the sigil at the peak; 6) forget it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBStatementIntent a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Statement of Intent"@en, "Absichtserklärung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make the magical intent clear and as precise as possible without overcomplicating it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBVagueIntentVagueResultFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vague intent, vague result"@en, "Vage Absicht, vages Ergebnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Vague intentions usually give vague results; the clearer the statement, the likelier fitting results."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a vague statement of intent usually brings a vague result. A rate word (usually) but no deadline; the failure is put on the operator's formulation."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"usually\")."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBStatementIntent."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBLoverSigilWithoutIntelligenceCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The lover sigil without intelligence"@en, "Die Liebhaber-Sigille ohne Intelligenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "An acquaintance made a sigil for a lover described in fine detail; he arrived exactly as described, but she had not asked for intelligence, and he talked of nothing but himself and his car."@en ;
    skos:note "Anecdote of a spell that worked too literally."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBStatementIntent ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 81; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDeconditioningEasesDisentanglingDesires a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deconditioning eases disentangling desires"@en, "Dekonditionierung erleichtert Entwirrung von Begehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "As a side effect of deconditioning, it gets steadily easier to tell apart one's habitual thoughts, feelings, desires and fantasies."@en ;
    skos:note "Deconditioning is treated earlier in the book, before Chapter Four."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 82; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEnchantSelectivelyHastySpellsComplicateCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Enchant selectively; hasty spells complicate"@en, "Selektiv zaubern; hastige Zauber verkomplizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians do not constantly cast spells for every desire; they enchant selectively and carefully because hasty enchantments often bring unforeseen complications."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 82; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDivinationExamineMotivesBehindDesire a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Divination to examine motives behind a desire"@en, "Divination zur Prüfung der Motive eines Begehrens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before enchanting, use a divination system of your choice (Tarot, Runes, I Ching) to examine the motives underlying a desire; accept answers that do not fit what you want."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 82; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBTarotReadingDissolvesComputerDesireYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tarot reading dissolves the computer desire"@en, "Tarotlegung löst den Computerwunsch auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine, entangled in frustrated desire for a new computer, consulted tarot: it advised against a loan, said he did not need a new machine and should repair the old one; he felt relief and insight into how desires take control."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDivinationExamineMotivesBehindDesire ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSelfInsightThroughAnalysingDesire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 82; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBIgnoringDivinationFoolsOnlyYourselfCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ignoring divination fools only yourself"@en, "Ignorierte Divination täuscht nur einen selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Be prepared for unwelcome answers; ignoring a divination shows you never wanted another perspective. Treat divination systems as trusted old friends whose advice you accept."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDivinationExamineMotivesBehindDesire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 83; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSWOT a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "SWOT analysis before enchanting"@en, "SWOT-Analyse vor dem Zaubern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Frame the surface statement of intent, then list: Strengths (pathways, information, best factor to influence), Weaknesses (what might block it), Opportunities (timing, situations raising chances), Threats (possible negative consequences). If weaknesses and threats outweigh, consider another approach."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 83; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSWOTRedirectsHelpSigilThatYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "SWOT redirects to a 'help' sigil that works"@en, "SWOT lenkt zu einer wirksamen 'Hilfe'-Sigille"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's SWOT showed that an enchantment to bring in a large sum of money faced more weaknesses and threats than strengths and opportunities, so he cast a sigil asking for help from others instead, and help came."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSWOT, pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBResultsMagicSigil ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 84; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBGatheringInformationBeforeSpell a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gathering information before a spell"@en, "Informationen vor einem Zauber sammeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask others' opinions and gather as much information as possible about the situation; e.g. Hine spent hours learning a client's habits, social movements and qualities before deciding what enchantment for meeting a partner to do and how it should act."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 84; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSorceryOthersHelpsPractice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sorcery for others helps one's practice"@en, "Zauberei für andere fördert die eigene Praxis"@de ;
    skos:definition "More information gives more flexibility in magical approach; performing sorcery on behalf of others is said to be very good for one's own practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 84; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBResultsMagicSigil a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Results magic by sigil"@en, "Ergebnismagie durch Sigillen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting exact results over a short or long term, in healing, changing habits, inspiration, steering dreams and so on, with sigils, instantly and almost anywhere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 84; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBOpeningPathwayIntent a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Opening a pathway for the intent"@en, "Einen Pfad für die Absicht öffnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make sure there is a possible route for the result to arrive by (for money: write a book, apply for a job, enter a lottery)."@en ;
    skos:note "Given in the text as generally considered useful."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 84; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFraterBatersMoneySpellFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Frater Bater's money spell"@en, "Frater Baters Geldzauber"@de ;
    skos:definition "Standard cautionary example: a money spell without an opened pathway brings money through relatives' sudden deaths and compensation for an industrial accident; the multiverse is said to have a slapstick sense of humour."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a money spell cast without an opened pathway brings money by unwelcome routes, the deaths of relatives and compensation for an accident. No deadline beyond the months of the example; put on the operator who opened no route, with the multiverse's humour named beside him."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBOpeningPathwayIntent."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 84; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBMonogramSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Monogram sigil"@en, "Monogramm-Sigille"@de ;
    skos:definition "Write out the intent, strike all repeated letters, and design a glyph from the remaining ones; this symbolic code can be attended to without recalling the desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 85; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBMantricSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Mantric sigil"@en, "Mantrische Sigille"@de ;
    skos:definition "Write out the intent and scramble it into a meaningless word or phrase to chant; or rearrange the letters into another sentence as mantra (e.g. a house-hunting intent becoming 'The Sun can Sing')."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 85; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilsOtherMedia a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigils in other media"@en, "Sigillen in anderen Medien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Carriers for the intent may also be smell, taste, colours, body language or hand gestures."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 85; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBGnosis a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Intense gnosis for sigil projection"@en, "Intensive Gnosis zur Sigillenprojektion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Send the sigil out through gnosis, usually but not always within ritual; ways in include spinning, chanting, dancing, visualisation, overload or deprivation of the senses, and sexual arousal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 85; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBIndifferentVacuity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Indifferent Vacuity"@en, "Gleichgültige Leere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enter a not-particularly-bothered state, e.g. doodling sigils while taking notes on a boring talk."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 85; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFiringSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Firing the sigil"@en, "Die Sigille abfeuern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Launch the sigil into the void at the height of gnosis or vacuity: at orgasm, at the edge of blacking out from hyperventilation, or when suddenly questioned on the dull lecture; or make it the theme of a conventional ritual; less conventionally, picture the glyph as a sneeze breaks, or at the moment of releasing a painfully full bladder."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 85; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBOrgasmEmpoweredSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Orgasm-empowered sigil"@en, "Durch Orgasmus aufgeladene Sigille"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the climax of orgasm (or where pain and pleasure turn into each other), see the sigil shine and then speed away into deep space; to affect a given person, picture it shining on their chest or on any organ easy to picture; a partner need not be told, though their help with stimulation is useful."@en ;
    skos:note "Presented as building on firing the sigil (pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFiringSigil)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 85; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBForgettingSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Forgetting the sigil"@en, "Die Sigille vergessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the sigil is fired, let the original intent go and leave the rest to the Butterfly Effect; when related thoughts come up, do not linger on them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 86; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBForgettingHardestPartCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Forgetting is the hardest part"@en, "Vergessen ist der schwerste Teil"@de ;
    skos:definition "Forgetting is often the hardest stage, especially when one really wants the outcome."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"often\")."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBForgettingSigil ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 86; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBStartSigilsThingsCareLittle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Start with sigils for things you care little about"@en, "Mit Sigillen für Unwichtiges beginnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beginning sigil experiments with desires one is not much attached to is recommended because they are easier to forget."@en ;
    skos:note "A recommended order for beginners; entered as a concept because the earlier step, sigils for intents one cares little about, has no node of its own and is not set apart in the text as a practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 86; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBGardenAnalogySigilisation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Garden analogy of sigilisation"@en, "Gartenanalogie der Sigillisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind's tangle of desires is likened to an unruly garden: sigilisation isolates and tends one plant until it stands out, then one loses interest and goes indoors; the trick is later not to notice that plant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 86; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBIntentTangledFantasiesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intent tangled with fantasies"@en, "Absicht mit Fantasien verstrickt"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the intent gets entangled with other mental content and one starts fantasising outcomes, the desire merges with others and the probability of it manifesting as wanted decreases."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: an intent tangled with fantasies of the outcome runs into the other desires, lowering the chance that it manifests as wanted. No deadline; a lowered probability, not a rate; the failure is put on the operator."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 86; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPostedCertainAttitude a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Posted-and-certain attitude"@en, "Abgeschickt-und-gewiss-Haltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once a sigil is sent to the multiverse, treat it as certain to work so no further effort is spent on it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 86; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBPriorSuccessBreedsSigilConfidencePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Prior success breeds sigil confidence"@en, "Früherer Erfolg erzeugt Sigillenvertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Such confidence tends to arise from having already had some success with sigils."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBResultsMagicSigil ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPostedCertainAttitude ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBResultArrivesWhenIntentLatentSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Result arrives when intent is latent"@en, "Ergebnis kommt, wenn die Absicht latent ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The result often turns up once the intent has sunk out of mind and been given up, as a lift comes on an empty road in the rain just after hope is lost."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the result comes once the intent has gone latent, forgotten and given up on. Hedged as what often happens; with no deadline, any later event can be read as the result."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"often\")."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBRecordingSigilExperiments a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Recording sigil experiments"@en, "Sigillenexperimente aufzeichnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Record experiments so the record does not bring the desire to mind: after writing up details, tape into the diary a scrap with the sigil on one side and the statement of intent pencilled on the other."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBatchSigilsDeliberatelyLost a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Batch sigils deliberately lost"@en, "Sigillen im Stapel absichtlich verlegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make six or so sigils together, file them and lose them on purpose; weeks later, when their desires are forgotten, pick one at random and charge it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDoodlingSigilsWhileBusy a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Doodling sigils while busy"@en, "Sigillen nebenbei kritzeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeatedly doodle a sigil while most attention is elsewhere; Hine finds the best time for sigil magic is when very busy, to avoid thinking about the desired effect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDwellingHopedEffectTrapCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Dwelling on the hoped-for effect as a trap"@en, "Falle, über die gewünschte Wirkung nachzudenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thinking about the desired effect is named a trap to avoid in sigil work."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilsEmbeddedMediaObjects a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigils embedded in media and objects"@en, "In Medien und Gegenstände eingebettete Sigillen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sigils can be built into photographs, cassette recordings, video, drawings, tattoos, earrings, wall-hangings and clothing designs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBLinkedSigils a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Linked sigils"@en, "Verknüpfte Sigillen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Prepare two sigils, one for the real desire and one for an easily forgotten sight (for example a red-haired woman carrying a small dog). Fire the second first, and carry the first about on a slip of paper. On noticing the person or thing described, the moment of recognition throws one into a brief burst of gnosis: fire the desire sigil then, for instance by seeing it whirl into a black chaosphere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 87; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBNoticingSigilisedSightingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Noticing the sigilised sighting"@en, "Bemerken des sigillierten Anblicks"@de ;
    skos:definition "Suddenly noticing the person or object described by the first sigil marks its working and the moment of gnosis for firing the second."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: one notices the person or object the first of the linked sigils was cast to show. Hedged as something that might well happen; no deadline is set for the sighting."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"might\")."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBLinkedSigils."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 88; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSwappingSigils a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Swapping sigils"@en, "Sigillen tauschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exchange sigils with another sigil-user so you hold a sigil meaningless to you and easily forgotten."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 88; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFramingIntentRelaxingAwayWhat a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Framing intent and relaxing away is what works"@en, "Absicht fassen und loslassen ist das Wirksame"@de ;
    skos:definition "Results tend to follow one's own intent even when another person fires a sigil one made; Hine reads this as showing that what matters is framing the statement and then relaxing away from the outcome, not hidden forces, symbols or energies."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"seems to indicate\")."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 88; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBExplanationCreatesContextNotTruth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Explanation creates context, not truth"@en, "Erklärung schafft Kontext, nicht Wahrheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A view arising in chaos magic: the explanation someone holds for an effect need not be accurate, yet it builds the setting in which the effect happens; the tangled metaphysics of modern magic gives a frame of belief inside which the magician can relax."@en ;
    skos:note "The role of belief in making a magical context is taken up in Chapter Seven."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 88; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRelaxationConfidenceKeys a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxation and confidence as keys"@en, "Entspannung und Vertrauen als Schlüssel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Relaxation and confidence are restated as the keys to magical success."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated as a requisite of magical practice as a whole; entered as a concept because the dependent step is magic in general, which has no node of its own. The text refers back to Chapter Three, where relaxation and confidence are treated."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 88; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAgainstProtestantWorkEthicMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the Protestant work ethic in magic"@en, "Gegen die protestantische Arbeitsethik in der Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine says the Protestant Work Ethic has permeated Western magic (rituals are called 'Workings'), whereas the chaos approach treats fun and pleasure as important, neglected sides of magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 88; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBMagicPlay a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic and play"@en, "Magie und Spiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magic and play both stand apart from ordinary life and lift one into the mythic; a child with a doll probably believes more readily than a sorcerer in his wax image; enchantments can be planned strictly and carried out playfully."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 89; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAPIE a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "A PIE"@en, "A PIE"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's sequence for sorcery: Assessment, Plan, Implementation, Evaluation."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 89; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPIEProcedure a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "A PIE procedure"@en, "A-PIE-Verfahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assessment: stop, do nothing, survey the situation and all options using divination, dream oracles, asking a favourite deity or visualising courses of action. Plan: decide what is needed (magical, material, financial resources, others' help, information and its source). Implementation: actually do it. Evaluation: look back to identify how will brought change, integrate experience, use the magical diary, be scrupulously honest."@en ;
    skos:note "Presented as building on a PIE (pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAPIE)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 89; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBInertiaImplementationHiddenFearCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Inertia at implementation as hidden fear"@en, "Trägheit bei der Umsetzung als verborgene Angst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Laziness and inertia may intervene at implementation, often as the surface of fear of failure or of success; each success gives momentum to the next."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"may\")."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPIEProcedure ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBHonestEvaluationDifficultCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Honest evaluation is difficult"@en, "Ehrliche Auswertung ist schwierig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evaluating results and techniques is often difficult without scrupulous honesty, a balance between the ideal manifestation and what actually happened."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"often\")."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPIEProcedure ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBNewSourcesPleasureSigilCountedYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "'New sources of pleasure' sigil counted success"@en, "Sigille 'neue Quellen der Freude' als Erfolg gewertet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine cast a sigil for new sources of pleasure (hoping for sex); a friend soon gave him computer games that gave many hours of pleasure, which he counted a success."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBResultsMagicSigil ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBMismatchSpecifiedIntentCountsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mismatch with specified intent counts as failure"@en, "Abweichung von der festgelegten Absicht gilt als Misserfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Had the intent explicitly specified sexual fulfilment and computer games arrived, Hine would count the enchantment a failure: success is judged against the stated intent."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a result that does not match an explicitly specified intent counts as a failure, as computer games would have against a stated sexual intent. No deadline or rate; the criterion is the operator's own statement of intent, and nothing is blamed."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBlamingKarmaFailedSpells a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No all-embracing explanation of failure"@en, "Keine allumfassende Erklärung für Misserfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is no general explanation for failed spells; Hine criticises the habit of blaming karma, destiny, cosmic tides, fate or the gods for failures while crediting successes to one's own ability."@en ;
    skos:note "Read at the text as a remark about how failures are explained, not as a condition of failure: it names no outcome that shows a spell did not work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRigorousPreparationRelaxedImplementation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rigorous preparation, relaxed implementation"@en, "Strenge Vorbereitung, entspannte Durchführung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Preparation and core procedure of sorcery depend on discipline, attention and awareness of consequences, which leaves one free to be relaxed about the actual technique."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 90; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPlasticineEnchantment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Plasticine enchantment"@en, "Knetmassen-Verzauberung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Form the letters of the statement of intent from plasticine strips; meditate on it; mash it into a ball; keep reshaping while hyperventilating and speaking in tongues; gouge and destroy sigils in it; entering gnosis, split it into halves (you and your desire) and mash them together at the climax. Reusable; may add nails, hair, blood."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCandleSpell a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Candle spell"@en, "Kerzenzauber"@de ;
    skos:definition "Carve sigils, runes or other signs into a candle and let it burn away while one gets on with something else; lovemaking in candlelight and further uses the spell books leave out are hinted at."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBStringKnotMagic a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "String and knot magic"@en, "Schnur- und Knotenmagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tie knots, or make webs, labyrinths and cat's cradles of string into which spells are whispered or which become the focus of an enchantment (as in modern witchcraft)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBraidedSacrificedHair a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Braided and sacrificed hair"@en, "Geflochtenes und geopfertes Haar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use plaited hair as an object of power, above all hair given up for a goal (a haircut to improve job chances); hair from dead relatives or associates readily takes on mythic power."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 91; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBGivens a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Givens and found objects"@en, "Gaben und Fundstücke"@de ;
    skos:definition "'Givens' are gifts significant through the circumstances or associations of receiving them that end up in one's toybox, power bundle or altar; found objects are things picked up for no reason and kept, for which a use eventually appears."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 92; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPhoneHandsetSummoningFriend a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Phone-handset summoning of a friend"@en, "Einen Freund per Telefonhörer-Fundstück rufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine carried a found piece of a telephone handset, and pretended to listen to a particular friend on it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 92; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCallingPersonMakeBelieve a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Calling a person by make-believe"@en, "Eine Person durch So-tun-als-ob herbeirufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Causing a particular person to turn up by make-believe contact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 92; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFriendAppearsWithinFiveMinutesYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Friend appears within five minutes"@en, "Freundin erscheint binnen fünf Minuten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whenever Hine pretended to chat to the friend on the old handset, she reliably arrived within five minutes."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPhoneHandsetSummoningFriend ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCallingPersonMakeBelieve ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 92; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDeliberateEffortDefeatsHandsetFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deliberate effort defeats the handset"@en, "Absichtliche Mühe vereitelt den Hörer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The harder Hine tried on purpose to call the friend with the handset, the less she tended to come."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: deliberate attempts to call the friend with the handset made her arrival less likely. Set against a reported five minutes for the successes; the failure is put on the operator's deliberate effort."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPhoneHandsetSummoningFriend."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 92; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAgainstNewAgeCrystalHype a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against New Age crystal hype"@en, "Gegen New-Age-Kristallrummel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine mocks claims that crystals cure, enable 'safe sex', gift Gaia, contact dolphins via ley lines or caused Atlantis' fall, and notes new-agers ignore their traditional use as spirit traps."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 92; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCrystalScryingTalismans a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Crystal scrying and talismans"@en, "Kristallschauen und Talismane"@de ;
    skos:definition "Crystals can serve for scrying (Dee is said to have used an obsidian ball) and as talismans, with symbolic meanings listed in crystal books."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 92; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBTrappingOrHousingEntityCrystal a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trapping or housing an entity in a crystal"@en, "Ein Wesen in einem Kristall fangen oder beherbergen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trapping an entity in a crystal, or making a crystal its home, is said to be quite possible; there are many old tales of spirits enticed into vessels."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"certainly possible\")."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 92; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSundryToyboxTools a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sundry toybox tools"@en, "Diverse Spielzeugkisten-Werkzeuge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dominoes and dice for divination; a lollipop stick with runes or sigils as a nondescript talisman; hammering a nail into wood as the physical act of an enchantment; chalk for circles, triangles and names; crayons for pictures and yantras."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 93; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPendulumWork a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulum work"@en, "Pendelarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calmly scan a room with a pendulum to find lost or hidden objects; dowse a map; answer simple yes/no questions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 93; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFindingLostObjects a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding lost objects"@en, "Verlorene Gegenstände finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Locating lost or hidden objects by divinatory means."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 93; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBPendulumFoundFriendsLostItemsYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulum found friends' lost items"@en, "Pendel fand verlorene Dinge von Freunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "On at least two occasions a calm pendulum scan found a friend's lost item in an unexpected place."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPendulumWork ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFindingLostObjects ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 93; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSimpleDivinationHasUses a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Simple divination has its uses"@en, "Einfache Divination hat ihren Nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is useful to divine without complex systems; even tea leaves, scorned by magicians, have their uses."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 93; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBalloonMagic a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Balloon magic"@en, "Ballonmagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blow into a balloon to project an intent; attach a sigil to a helium balloon and release it; burst a balloon to climax a ritual; use colour correspondences; shape balloons into fetishes or animals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 93; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFindingPixie a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The finding pixie"@en, "Der Findewichtel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine gave a ceramic pixie from a holiday the power of finding mislaid things: when something was lost he asked the pixie and went on searching; once it turned up he thanked the pixie, now and then leaving a silver coin beneath it; others in the house were talked into doing the same."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 94; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBPixieNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The pixie"@en, "Der Wichtel"@de ;
    skos:definition "A ceramic pixie figure endowed by Hine with the function of finding lost household objects and thanked with silver coins; called a very basic magical evocation."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "the pixie" ;
    pm:nameRole "finder spirit housed in a figure" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 94; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBPixieRoutineWorkedWellYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Pixie routine worked well"@en, "Wichtel-Routine wirkte gut"@de ;
    skos:definition "Over time the ask-and-thank routine worked very well."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFindingPixie ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFindingLostObjects ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 94; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFeedingSpiritAttribution a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeding a spirit by attribution"@en, "Einen Geist durch Zuschreibung nähren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nourish a spirit by crediting every success within its field to it and by building a relationship with it; Hine finds this the most effective way."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 94; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFiveMagicalWeaponsReinterpreted a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five magical weapons, reinterpreted"@en, "Fünf magische Waffen, neu gedeutet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's reading of the formal weapons of modern magic: Wand (projected will, unity of desire, initial drive), Dagger (analysis and discrimination), Chalice (receptive transmission, unhindered perception), Pentacle (synthesis, manifestation of results), Lamp (inspiration). No heaps of symbolism needed to use them."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 94; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBOathsAbstentionsBreedInnerConflictCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Oaths and abstentions breed inner conflict"@en, "Eide und Enthaltungen erzeugen inneren Konflikt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Oaths, promises and abstentions only set the mind against itself; the magician looks for unity of desire before acting, which is why preparation matters."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBOathsStringentTestsFailFailure ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 94; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDaggerOnlyGoodDiscrimination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dagger only as good as one's discrimination"@en, "Dolch nur so gut wie das eigene Unterscheidungsvermögen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The dagger, an extension of the finger for drawing symbols in the air, embodies analysis and discrimination; any dagger is only as effective as one's own skill at these, hence planning and breaking goals into steps."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 94; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBChargedChalicePentacleCharging a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Charged chalice and pentacle charging"@en, "Geladener Kelch und Laden auf dem Pentakel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wine or other fluid in the chalice is first charged by invocation and then drunk by the celebrants; the chalice can also be used for scrying; objects to be charged with power are placed on the pentacle in ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 95; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBHolyGuardianAngelNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Holy Guardian Angel / Godhead as Lamp"@en, "Heiliger Schutzengel / Gottheit als Lampe"@de ;
    skos:definition "In traditional Western magic Godhead and the Holy Guardian Angel are said to be two aspects of the Lamp, the weapon of inspiration; a primitive fetish or a symbol tied to gnosis could fill the same role."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Holy Guardian Angel" ;
    pm:nameRole "source of inspiration (Lamp aspect)" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 95; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBAcquiringMagicalWeapons a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Acquiring magical weapons"@en, "Magische Waffen erwerben"@de ;
    skos:definition "By an old saying, weapons should be made by their owner, received as gifts, or found in strange ways; saving up to buy one, the more so at some cost to oneself (such as walking to work), also makes it special. The qualities matter more than the objects."@en ;
    skos:note "Given in the text as an old adage."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 95; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWeaponsOperatingOutsideRitual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Weapons operating outside ritual"@en, "Waffen außerhalb des Rituals"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine maps the weapons onto writing: desire and decision to write = wand; language ordering thought = dagger; the screen prompting ideas = chalice; the printout = pentacle; any illuminatory technique aiding creativity = lamp."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 95; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBPracticeSuspendedDisbeliefGnosisPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Practice, suspended disbelief and gnosis"@en, "Übung, aufgehobener Unglaube und Gnosis"@de ;
    skos:definition "As with games, success in sorcery depends more on the player's skill than on equipment, and it needs practice, a willing suspension of disbelief, and gnosis, a halt of inner talk lasting from seconds to hours."@en ;
    skos:note "Practice and suspension of disbelief are named beside gnosis as requirements; only gnosis has a node here."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondBGnosis ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBResultsMagicSigil ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 96; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBResponsiveSorcery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Responsive sorcery; easiest route"@en, "Reagierende Zauberei; leichtester Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sorcery has to adapt as one's life changes; it is less a way of getting something for nothing than of being as effective as possible in each area of life; magic is often said to take the path of least resistance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 96; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBJobSpellWithoutConfidenceFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Job spell without confidence"@en, "Jobzauber ohne Selbstvertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Casting for a new job is pointless if lack of confidence will ruin every interview."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: enchanting for a new job is pointless when lack of confidence will spoil every interview. No deadline or rate; the failure is put on the operator."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilMagicFullProcess."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 96; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBProtectionAttention a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Protection by attention"@en, "Schutz durch Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "First ask what protection means and why you want it; if clumsy or inattentive, use techniques that drag attention to your surroundings and cultivate the danger/alert sense (Chapter Three)."@en ;
    skos:note "The danger or alert sense it refers to is treated in Chapter Three."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 96; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBNoMagicalAttack a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No magical attack"@en, "Kein magischer Angriff"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine says there is no magical attack to worry about: ninety-nine percent is self-inflicted, and those who talk of it usually hide some inadequacy and inflated self-importance; a tuned warning sense and groundedness are more use."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 96; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBObsessionMagicalAttackCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Obsession with magical attack"@en, "Besessenheit von magischem Angriff"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some become concerned with protection against magical attack to an obsessive degree."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBNoMagicalAttack ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 96; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBindingPartingLovers a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Binding and parting lovers"@en, "Liebende vereinen und trennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bringing lovers together or parting them, part of what a sorcerer is held able to do, which is why sorcerers are at once respected and feared."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 97; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBObservationNonverbalReadingLoveMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Observation and nonverbal reading for love magic"@en, "Beobachtung und nonverbales Lesen für Liebesmagie"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the most basic level it helps to observe closely, read unspoken signals and judge when to talk and when to be quiet; love magic deals with other people."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated as what helps at a basic level in love magic; entered as a concept because the skills named have no node of their own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 97; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBLoveSpellsAimedParticularPersonFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love spells aimed at a particular person"@en, "Liebeszauber auf eine bestimmte Person"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine reports that love spells aimed at one particular person never turn out well."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: love spells aimed at one particular person never turn out well, in Hine's experience. A rate word (never) but no deadline; the failure is put on the method of aiming at a person."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBEnchantingLoverNeed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 97; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBEnchantingLoverNeed a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Enchanting for the lover you need"@en, "Für den Liebhaber zaubern, den man braucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Be clear whether a passing sexual encounter or a relationship is wanted, see that one's picture of an ideal lover depends on circumstance and differs from what one needs, and cast for the lover one needs, not the one one wants."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 97; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBLoveSpellsNotInnocuousCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Love spells are not innocuous"@en, "Liebeszauber sind nicht harmlos"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine finds it odd that love spells are thought innocuous while curses are condemned, since involvement with someone can itself be a curse; before magically meddling in others' relationships, consider how you would feel if done to you."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBindingPartingLovers ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 97; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBOwnAttractionOverSpells a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Own attraction over spells"@en, "Eigene Anziehung statt Zauber"@de ;
    skos:definition "Though one can influence people into sex, working on one's own seduction and attraction is more effective long-term; spells alone cannot overcome a lack of charisma unless other qualities are enhanced toward the goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 97; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBMagicalHealing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical healing"@en, "Magisches Heilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Healing clients by magical means; an accomplished healer gets noticed; said to need much further work and investigation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 98; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAgainstExoticNewAgeHealing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against exotic new-age healing"@en, "Gegen exotisches New-Age-Heilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine tells would-be healers to leave aside past-life regression, aura diagnosis, chakra massage and the new-age healing trade, and to aim only at the client getting better; practical healing lived on in witchcraft and spiritualism, not in the mainstream of Western occultism."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 98; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBHealerPersona a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Healer persona"@en, "Heiler-Persona"@de ;
    skos:definition "Develop a healer persona to project a certain ambience and keep professional distance from clients (see Ego Magic)."@en ;
    skos:note "The healer persona is referred on to Ego Magic, Chapter Seven."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 98; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBObsessiveDesireHealCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Obsessive desire to heal"@en, "Zwanghafter Heilwunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting to be a healer is to be examined hard now and then, since it can turn obsessive, until one guards one's image as a healer more than one serves the clients."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBMagicalHealing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 98; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAgainstCondemningCurses a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against condemning curses"@en, "Gegen die Verurteilung von Flüchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine disputes the common view that cursing is wrong, unethical or brings karmic consequences: curses are ancient and sophisticated in tribal societies and are thrown when other retaliation is impossible; life is more complex than white/black magic dichotomies."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 98; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBConditionsBeforeCursingCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Conditions before cursing"@en, "Bedingungen vor dem Verfluchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before cursing, make sure that it really is the fittest course, that one can bear whatever follows, and that it will bring the result wanted; work out one's own rules."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a caution: the three conditions are things to be sure of before cursing, not earlier steps with nodes of their own."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCursing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 99; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCursing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cursing"@en, "Verfluchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Offensive magic, for example making a serial rapist ever clumsier until he is caught; Hine also asks whether a requiem said at a distance for a dying friend who wished to die would be wrong."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 99; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWealthBeyondMoney a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wealth beyond money; deceptive desire"@en, "Reichtum mehr als Geld; trügerisches Begehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wealth is something one either strives for or has; money is just one part of wealth magic; desires, sexual desire among them, are misleading, complex and liable to sudden change."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 99; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSexualDesireCanDangerousCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Sexual desire can be dangerous"@en, "Sexuelles Begehren kann gefährlich sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sexual desire can change without warning and be perilous; much turns on whether the ego comes through such shifts."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWealthBeyondMoney ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 100; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWealthFameGlamours a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wealth and fame as glamours"@en, "Reichtum und Ruhm als Blendwerke"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wealth and fame are called glamours: desires that hold us because we feel something is missing and are uneasy with how things are; wealth magic is too vague and too distant an aim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSolarConfidenceBeforeJovianExpansivenessPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Solar confidence before Jovian expansiveness"@en, "Solares Selbstvertrauen vor jovialer Weite"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must work with confidence, the Solar quality, before the Jovian quality of expansiveness, which is linked to wealth magic, can be reached."@en ;
    skos:note "The dependent step is Jovian expansiveness, which appears only as one sphere inside the ordering of magics bearing on wealth."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBConfidenceSkill ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSpheresMagicWealth ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Expansiveness cannot be reached while one is in conflict with oneself." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBConfidenceSkill a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence as skill"@en, "Selbstvertrauen als Fertigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Confidence understood as a skill: being at ease in the present moment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRelaxationHiddenKeySuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxation as hidden key to success"@en, "Entspannung als verborgener Erfolgsschlüssel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Relaxation is called the unrecognised key to success in magic: when relaxed one is free of past patterns, no longer casts desires ahead, and sees situations as they are."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBConfidenceNeedsSelfLoveNeedsPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence needs self-love needs self-awareness"@en, "Selbstvertrauen braucht Selbstliebe braucht Selbsterkenntnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Confidence requires some self-love, which requires self-awareness, especially of one's nested desire-complexes."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSelfInsightThroughAnalysingDesire ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBConfidenceSkill ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSurfaceDesiresEgoBlindsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Surface desires as ego blinds"@en, "Oberflächenwünsche als Ich-Tarnungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Surface desires often serve the ego as screens for what cannot be faced; such hidden conflicts end by undoing the magician (as with a desire disguised behind a respectable role with the young)."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSelfInsightThroughAnalysingDesire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 101; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSelfAcceptanceBeforeAcceptingOthersPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-acceptance before accepting others"@en, "Selbstannahme vor Annahme anderer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Until you accept yourself you cannot accept others as independent beings."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-acceptance is read as the self-love of the Solar quality, entered with confidence; accepting others as the dynamics of love magic, entered with the sorcerer's power over lovers."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBConfidenceSkill ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBindingPartingLovers ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without accepting oneself one keeps being let down whenever others do not behave as one thinks they should." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSpheresMagicWealth a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spheres of magic for wealth"@en, "Sphären der Magie für Reichtum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's cluster of planetary/thematic magics bearing on wealth: Solar (confidence, self-love), Love (interacting with others), Jupiter (expansiveness), Mars (energy, drive, discipline, cool poise), Thought (planning, contingencies, resources), Death (killing unfeasible plans; boundaries), Sexual/Yesod (seduction, glamour, illusion); Business Magic applies these rays to one's work."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBNeedingStatusGoodsFeelSexyCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Needing status goods to feel sexy"@en, "Statusgüter brauchen, um sich sexy zu fühlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If you need fast clothes, big cars or attractive partners to feel sexy, something may be going wrong; attractiveness is rooted in self-love."@en ;
    skos:note "The roots in self-love are referred on to Ego Magic, Chapter Seven."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSpheresMagicWealth ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDwellingWealthRemindsLackFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dwelling on wealth reminds of lack"@en, "Grübeln über Reichtum erinnert an Mangel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Don't dwell on desired wealth: by an old axiom what binds you is never attained; the Unconscious (Spare's 'greatest magician') does not grasp this, and each wish for wealth reminds you of what you lack; declaring you want fame makes you a prat."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: dwelling on a desire for wealth keeps it out of reach, since each wish reminds one of lack and, by an old axiom, what binds you is never attained. No deadline or rate; the failure is put on the operator's attachment."@en ;
    skos:note "The condition bears on enchanting for wealth or fame; Hine sends the reader instead to the other spheres of magic and to business magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBusinessMagicImpressionManagement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Business magic and impression management"@en, "Geschäftsmagie und Eindrucksmanagement"@de ;
    skos:definition "Work through the other spheres instead: learn about people, about leading, managing and inspiring, and about getting one's will done; learn how doors are opened, whom to approach and when, and the craft of impression management."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 102; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBEmperorArchetypeStudy a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Emperor archetype study"@en, "Studium des Kaiser-Archetyps"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use the Emperor, Prince or Mandarin as archetype: read Machiavelli, study imperial figures, note how emperors use resources, give generously, and generate respect; find out how to win others' respect, and do it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWealthSiddha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wealth as siddha; powers as byproducts"@en, "Reichtum als Siddhi; Kräfte als Nebenprodukte"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Indian tradition wealth, like wisdom, is a siddha, something reached by degrees; on the Tantric path all magical powers are by-products of living one's life, often credited to the magician by others before he sees them himself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBGaneshaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Ganesha"@en, "Ganesha"@de ;
    skos:definition "A useful deity who brings wealth without being attached to or weighed down by it; relaxed in the world."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Ganesha" ;
    pm:nameRole "deity of wealth" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBWealthEnjoymentPresentCircumstances a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wealth as enjoyment of present circumstances"@en, "Reichtum als Genuss der gegenwärtigen Umstände"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine defines wealth magic as learning to see and take pleasure in one's present situation; expansiveness, glossed as high spirits, generosity and readiness to talk, implies ease in the present."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEmptyHandedGesture a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Empty-Handed Gesture"@en, "Die Geste der leeren Hand"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sign of an advanced sorcerer: sorcery done without objects or formal setting, perhaps with gestures alone, using visualisation and make-believe to open the space for magic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSkillsEmptyHandedGesturePrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Skills for the Empty-Handed Gesture"@en, "Fertigkeiten für die Geste der leeren Hand"@de ;
    skos:definition "The skills required: trained visualisation, a quiet confidence stopping short of arrogance, and the ability to release a desire from the ego-complex, all of them built up first through formal sorcery."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBVisualisationProficiency, pmc:ChaosMagicCondBConfidenceSkill ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEmptyHandedGesture ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSeemingLuckSuccessfulSorcererSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeming luck of the successful sorcerer"@en, "Scheinbares Glück des erfolgreichen Zauberers"@de ;
    skos:definition "A successful sorcerer need not display wealth but tends to look lucky, turning up where and when things happen."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the successful sorcerer tends to look lucky, turning up where and when things happen, rather than displaying wealth. No rate; the text adds at once that claimed high success rates probably reflect selective enchanting."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"tends to\")."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 103; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBNoticingPatternsCoincidence a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Noticing patterns and coincidence"@en, "Muster und Zufälle bemerken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pay attention to what happens in your life, noting hidden patterns in everyday chaos and acknowledging fortuitous coincidences."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 104; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBHighSuccessRatesReflectSelectivityCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "High success rates reflect selectivity"@en, "Hohe Erfolgsquoten spiegeln Auswahl"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sorcerer claiming a high success rate is probably selective about what he enchants for."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"chances are\")."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSeemingLuckSuccessfulSorcererSign ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 5 Playing with Chaos, p. 104; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .


#
# Chapter Six, Chaos Servitors
#

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEvocation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evocation"@en, "Evokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evocation, a calling forth, covers every technique that brings an entity into a bounded space, a bottle, a crystal or a pictured form with shape and character, usually to have it carry out a task."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 105; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEvocationNeitherLesserNorWrong a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evocation is neither lesser nor wrong"@en, "Evokation ist weder niedrig noch falsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine rejects both the view that evocation for tasks, linked with the demons of grimoires like the Keys of Solomon, is unspiritual lesser magic, and the view that magicians ought not to command spirits; he calls evocation a very useful technique."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 105; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBServitorNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Servitor"@en, "Servitor"@de ;
    skos:definition "An entity deliberately made by evocatory means to carry out a task or service; called a thought-form in the Western Esoteric Tradition and a tulpa in Tibetan magic; usable for many kinds of task."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Servitor" ;
    pm:nameRole "created task-entity" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 105; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBServitorsPerformingTasksBehalf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Servitors performing tasks on one's behalf"@en, "Servitoren, die Aufgaben für einen erledigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having made entities carry out tasks for one, such as healing, protecting, binding, bringing harmony or luck, divining or lifting moods."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 105; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBServitorDesignSequence a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Servitor Design Sequence"@en, "Servitor-Entwurfssequenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's seven-step design scheme treating servitors cybernetically as programmable astral machines: 1) general intent; 2) specific intent; 3) symbols; 4) time factor; 5) name; 6) material base; 7) shape."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 105; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDesigningServitor a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Designing a servitor"@en, "Einen Servitor entwerfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "1) Define the general sphere (healing, protection, binding, luck, divination, mood...) and gather associations, optionally chains of correspondences from a book like 777. 2) Formulate the specific Statement of Intent (its 'aetheric DNA') after self-analysis, SWOT or divination, and render it as a sigil. 3) Embellish the sigil with fitting symbols (colour, smell, sound too). 4) Decide duration and timing (moon phases, planetary hours) and what happens after the task. 5) Optionally name it. 6) Optionally give it a material base. 7) Choose a shape."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 106; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBExampleHealingServitorsSigil a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Example: the Healing Servitor's sigil"@en, "Beispiel: Sigille des Heil-Servitors"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement of intent for rapid recovery and health of a named person, turned into a sigil; the sigil set within a hexagram (balance, health, solar quality; union of Fire for burning fever and Water for sweating out toxins and calming) with the number 7 (harmony and duration); the whole figure forms the instructions visualised as part of the servitor at launch."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 107; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDeepMindOceanSelfIceberg a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deep Mind as ocean, self as iceberg"@en, "Tiefengeist als Ozean, Selbst als Eisberg"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Deep Mind is likened to an ocean dotted with islands of selves; each self is an iceberg mostly below awareness, a lattice of psychic structures (Personal, Social, Mythic) from internalised experience; 'embedded' structures form the world-view below the surface; magic is said to work by heating the iceberg from within so it becomes more responsive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 107; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSymbolsSharedLanguageWakingDeep a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Symbols as shared language of waking and Deep Mind"@en, "Symbole als gemeinsame Sprache von Wachbewusstsein und Tiefengeist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deeper experience is encoded as symbols, non-linguistic figures that encapsulate emotions and memories freed when focused on; symbols are the language shared by waking awareness and Deep Mind; magical systems embed symbol sets, exercises like tarot meditation fix them, and the Deep Mind clothes its insights in them; some symbols seem universal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBMeditationTarotImages a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation on tarot images"@en, "Meditation über Tarotbilder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meditate on tarot card images so as to fix their symbols in the mind, giving the Deep Mind a vocabulary in which to communicate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSymbolFixingYieldsDeepMindYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Symbol fixing yields Deep-Mind communication"@en, "Symbolfixierung ergibt Kommunikation mit dem Tiefengeist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exercises that fix symbols enable the Deep Mind to use them to convey insights."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"often\")."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBMeditationTarotImages ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDeepMindCommunicatingThroughSymbols ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDeepMindCommunicatingThroughSymbols a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deep Mind communicating through symbols"@en, "Tiefengeist teilt sich durch Symbole mit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting insight and information from the Deep Mind dressed in symbols it has absorbed; symbols open layers of the Deep Mind and charged memories more directly and intensely than words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSoundSmellColourSymbols a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sound, smell and colour as symbols"@en, "Klang, Geruch und Farbe als Symbole"@de ;
    skos:definition "Besides graphic designs, sound, smell and colour act as symbol-carriers with powerful, often unnoticed effects and associations, important in magical practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 109; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBThreeCategoriesGraphicSymbols a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three categories of graphic symbols"@en, "Drei Kategorien grafischer Symbole"@de ;
    skos:definition "Graphic magical figures fall into: i) those derived from magical or religious systems (planetary signs, pentagram, secret alphabets); ii) those made by the magician for a purpose (sigils); iii) those arising from the Deep Mind. Personal or discovered symbols are generally held more beneficial, though systemic ones may be used."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 110; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBServitorTimingInstructions a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Servitor timing instructions"@en, "Zeitanweisungen für Servitoren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Settle whether the servitor is to work all the time or only at certain times, and write moon phases, conjunctions or planetary hours into its instructions; the healing servitor, for example, was to work for seven days, for seven minutes every seven hours."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 110; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBTaskSpecificGeneralPurposeServitors a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Task-specific and general-purpose servitors"@en, "Aufgabenspezifische und Allzweck-Servitoren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Servitors are generally of two forms: task-specific and general-purpose."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 110; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSelfDestructClause a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-destruct clause"@en, "Selbstzerstörungsklausel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Encode at creation an instruction that the servitor's existence ends with its task or a stated condition, e.g. ending the healing intent with a phrase making the sum of the 7/7/7 intervals its lifespan."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 111; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBRitualReabsorptionServitor a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual reabsorption of a servitor"@en, "Rituelle Rücknahme eines Servitors"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mentally draw the servitor back from its task, take it apart by visualisation, take back the desire that sparked it, and dismantle or destroy any material base."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 111; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBUntendedThoughtFormsReclaimResponsibilityCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Untended thought-forms; reclaim responsibility"@en, "Unbetreute Gedankenformen; Verantwortung zurücknehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Disassembling a servitor after its task is generally preferred: classical occult theory says neglected thought-forms wander the astral annoying people, and psychologically one thereby reclaims responsibility for the desire-complex used."@en ;
    skos:note "Given in the text as generally held."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDesigningServitor ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 111; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBNamingBaseScentShapeServitor a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Naming, base, scent and shape of a servitor"@en, "Name, Basis, Duft und Gestalt eines Servitors"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give a name (reflecting the task or a mantric sigil of the intent) to create, power or control it; optionally give a material base (bottle, ring, crystal, figurine, modelling compound), possibly with bodily fluids to strengthen the link; or leave it aetheric (Hine: one-shot servitors aetheric, long-term ones based); or link it to a state of consciousness; or link it to a perfume or oil that activates it (dab on the base, inhale during launch); choose any shape, commonly a featureless pulsing sphere in chosen colours impressed with its sigil."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 111; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBTUMMYHUMNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "TUMMYHUM"@en, "TUMMYHUM"@de ;
    skos:definition "Name given to Hine's example healing servitor, a whimsical reference to its function."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "TUMMYHUM" ;
    pm:nameRole "healing servitor" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 111; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDesignLaunchYieldWorkingServitorYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Design and launch yield a working servitor"@en, "Entwurf und Start ergeben einen wirkenden Servitor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The design sequence followed by a launch produces a servitor able to act within its sphere."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDesigningServitor, pmp:ChaosMagicCondBNamingBaseScentShapeServitor, pmp:ChaosMagicCondBAirburstServitorLaunch ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBServitorsPerformingTasksBehalf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 112; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBServitorLaunchProcedure a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Servitor Launch Procedure"@en, "Servitor-Startverfahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "An introductory launch in five steps: banishing; statement of intent; the Lightning Flash; the Airburst launch; a second banishing."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 112; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBanishingRitualCrossLightPentagrams a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing ritual (Cross of Light and pentagrams)"@en, "Bannungsritual (Lichtkreuz und Pentagramme)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stand facing east, arms down, head a little raised, breathing slowly; empty the mind. 1) Breathing in, raise the right hand and picture a point of light above the fingertips. 2) Draw the hand down the middle of the body to point between the feet, breathing out, seeing white light run from above the head to below the feet. 3) Breathing in, spread the arms as a Tau; breathing out, see light cross the body sideways. 4) Breathing in, cross the arms over the chest; breathing out, see light spread from both lines; breathe deeply and feel charged (the Cross of Light). 5) Breathing in, draw a pentagram in the air, apex to lower left, to right, to left, to lower right, back to apex; breathing out, vibrate IAO and see the pentagram blaze white. 6) Do the same to south, west and north. 7) Raise the arms and recite a litany of five-pointed stars about one, endless stars overhead, and a ring of stars."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBanishingRitualCrossLightPentagramsYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing ritual (Cross of Light and pentagrams) yields being centred and poised"@en, "Bannungsritual (Lichtkreuz und Pentagramme) ergibt Zentriert und handlungsbereit sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The banishing is said to leave the operator centred within the ritual space, ready for the statement of intent."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBanishingRitualCrossLightPentagrams ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBeingCentredPoised ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBChargedEnergyAfterCrossLightSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Charged with energy after Cross of Light"@en, "Nach dem Lichtkreuz mit Energie geladen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Breathing deeply and feeling charged with energy marks completion of the first stage."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: breathing deeply and feeling charged with energy at the close of the Cross of Light. Given inside the instruction itself; no deadline or rate."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBanishingRitualCrossLightPentagrams."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBLaunchStatementIntent a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Launch Statement of Intent"@en, "Absichtserklärung beim Start"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once centred in the ritual space, declare the intent, for instance that one wills to evoke a servitor for a stated mission."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 113; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBLightningFlashExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Lightning Flash exercise"@en, "Blitzschlag-Übung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Loosely based on the Qabalistic Middle Pillar. 1) Stand feet apart, arms up, eyes closed, head tilted up. 2) Visualise yourself as a lone oak on a bleak night landscape under stars, breathing slow, rooted yet reaching. 3) A storm builds; quicken breathing; wind shakes you; electric tension, throbbing earth. 4) Build to fever pitch, breath fast and shallow, rock forward straining and shaking. 5) When unbearable, a lightning bolt strikes, you shudder and its energy runs down through your roots into the earth. 6) An answering surge rises from deep earth, up your body, carrying consciousness into the sky as a star. 7) Lower arms, feet together, two fingers of right hand to lips."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 114; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBLightningFlashEnergisesYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Lightning Flash energises"@en, "Blitzschlag energetisiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercise combining breath, visualisation, body awareness and build-up and discharge of tension energises the practitioner."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBLightningFlashExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSelfEnergising ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 114; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSelfEnergising a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-energising"@en, "Selbstenergetisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being calm yet supercharged with energy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 114; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCalmYetSuperchargedSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Calm yet supercharged"@en, "Ruhig und doch hochgeladen"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the end of the Lightning Flash one should feel calm yet supercharged with energy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: feeling calm yet charged with energy at the close of the Lightning Flash. Given inside the instruction itself; no deadline or rate."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBLightningFlashExercise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 114; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBAirburstServitorLaunch a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Airburst servitor launch"@en, "Airburst-Servitorstart"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drawn from the Wiccan raising of the cone of power, and usable by groups. 1) Sit comfortably (the Dragon asana is ideal) and breathe easily. 2) Feel full of energy and let it gather into a white sphere at the solar plexus. 3) Let a cord of light extend from there to two feet or more ahead. 4) Let it rise into a pulsing column and then stand free, cut off from oneself. 5) Concentrate on its top until it swells into a sphere that pulls the whole column up into itself. 6) Programme it: give it its shape, merge its instruction symbols into it, chant its name as a mantra to feed it, flash chosen colours, or see its sigils as DNA growing into cells, muscle and nerves, or its body built from chains of sigils. 7) Breathe faster toward a climax and count down from ten, the servitor throbbing like a heart and the work growing frenzied; at one, breathe in deeply, shout BLAST OFF, see it rocket away and let oneself collapse. 8) Rest, and banish again if needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Presented as building on banishing ritual (Cross of Light and pentagrams) (pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBanishingRitualCrossLightPentagrams), launch Statement of Intent (pmp:ChaosMagicCondBLaunchStatementIntent), lightning Flash exercise (pmp:ChaosMagicCondBLightningFlashExercise)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 114; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBGeneralPurposeServitorsLearningExpert a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "General-purpose servitors as learning expert systems"@en, "Allzweck-Servitoren als lernende Expertensysteme"@de ;
    skos:definition "A servitor with a general provenance (e.g. healing, not one person) acts like an expert system that seems to get better with each task; continued successful use builds users' confidence, and anyone knowing its activation sequence (mantra, sigil, visualisation) can employ it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 116; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBICANDOONaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "ICANDOO"@en, "ICANDOO"@de ;
    skos:definition "A servitor ('I-can-do') created by twelve people at an open workshop, summoned by its name as mantra, briefed to help users overcome any obstacles, and designed to divide itself holographically so each segment held all its powers; all participants used it through the day."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "ICANDOO" ;
    pm:nameRole "general-purpose obstacle-clearing group servitor" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 116; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBoostingSuccessOwnMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Boosting the success of one's own magic"@en, "Steigerung des Erfolgs der eigenen Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Servitors with no task except to raise the success rate of one's magic, of use in enchanting, divining and illumination."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 116; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBGoHuNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "GoHu"@en, "GoHu"@de ;
    skos:definition "A servitor in the form of a dark, slightly hollowed mirror, woken by visualisation and mantra; sigilised desires were sent into it, and seen from another angle as a bowl it gave off ideas and images; Hine often woke it before using divination."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "GoHu" ;
    pm:nameRole "general magic-enhancing servitor" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 116; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFeedingServitor a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeding a servitor"@en, "Einen Servitor nähren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each use feeds a servitor and each result rated a success enhances its power; make a habit of attributing any occurrence within its sphere to its work."@en ;
    skos:note "Given in the text as generally held."@en ;
    skos:note "Presented as building on feeding a spirit by attribution (pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFeedingSpiritAttribution)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 117; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBServitorDependencyEurekaOffLineFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Servitor dependency (Eureka off-line)"@en, "Servitor-Abhängigkeit (Eureka abgeschaltet)"@de ;
    skos:definition "When Eureka went off-line on 22 April 1993 as Neptune and Uranus turned retrograde, Hine found creative flow much harder: the servitor had become so dominant in his creative process that he had become dependent on it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: when the illumination servitor went off-line on the date its activity had been tied to (22 April 1993, as Neptune and Uranus turned retrograde), creative flow became much harder for Hine. A dated end set by the operator; the failure is put on the operator's dependence on the servitor."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFeedingServitor."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 117; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAttributionCanBreedDependencyCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Attribution can breed dependency"@en, "Zuschreibung kann Abhängigkeit erzeugen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attributing all occurrences in a sphere to a servitor can lead to problems such as dependency; Hine now only occasionally uses a surviving fragment."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFeedingServitor ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 117; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEurekaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Eureka"@en, "Eureka"@de ;
    skos:definition "A servitor Hine made in 1992 for illumination, meaning inspiration, fresh ideas, creativity and brainstorming; with a colleague it acted as a Third Mind growing out of their talk; its working was later linked to the Neptune-Uranus conjunction."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Eureka" ;
    pm:nameRole "illumination servitor" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 117; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEurekaExceededExpectationsYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Eureka exceeded expectations"@en, "Eureka übertraf die Erwartungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Initially Eureka exceeded all Hine's expectations, stimulating ideas for writing, lecturing and workshops; each creative leap boosted its power."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDesigningServitor, pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFeedingServitor ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBConnectivityCreativeLeaps ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 117; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDisassemblingSurvivingSplinter a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Disassembling with a surviving splinter"@en, "Zerlegen mit verbleibendem Splitter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Call a servitor back and take it apart in a way that leaves a fragment of its power as an occasional focus (as was done with Eureka)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 117; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBViralSelfReplicatingServitors a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Viral (self-replicating) servitors"@en, "Virale (sich vermehrende) Servitoren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tell a servitor to multiply, by something like the division of cells on cybernetic or viral lines, or to give birth when set conditions arise, such as units of time, astrological transits or a given act by the target."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 117; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBViralServitorRecoversWithheldPropertyYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Viral servitor recovers withheld property"@en, "Viraler Servitor erwirkt Rückgabe einbehaltenen Eigentums"@de ;
    skos:definition "In an early test a servitor sent to recover withheld property generated a confusion field (lost keys, electrical blowouts) after a first deadline and replicated after a second, intensifying into poltergeist-like events; when the property was returned the servitors ceased; evidence was gathered from the target's associates."@en ;
    skos:note "The operator of the test is not named."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBViralSelfReplicatingServitors ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEscalatingPressureReplicatingServitors ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 117; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEvidenceAssociatesTargetSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence from associates of the target"@en, "Belege von Bekannten des Ziels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Success was checked by talking to the target's associates about intensifying minor problems; cessation upon return of property."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: minor troubles around the target growing into poltergeist-like events, learned by talking to the target's associates, and stopping when the property was returned. The deadlines were set in the servitor's instructions; the evidence is report from the target's circle."@en ;
    skos:note "It bears on pmp:ChaosMagicCondBViralSelfReplicatingServitors."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEscalatingPressureReplicatingServitors a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Escalating pressure by replicating servitors"@en, "Eskalierender Druck durch sich vermehrende Servitoren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Producing intensifying confusion around a target until a condition is met; viral servitors are suited to long-term enchantments such as raising the success probability of one's magic, healing and general protection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBChaoMines a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating Chao-Mines"@en, "Chao-Minen erzeugen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using servitor techniques, form a localised aetheric store and transmitter of chaos energy visualised as a spheroid with eight arrows or antennae flashing randomly in all colours, placed at sites of habitual magical activity or good vibes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCreatingChaoMinesYieldsProbabilityYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Creating Chao-Mines yields probability tilted toward the fortuitous"@en, "Chao-Minen erzeugen ergibt Wahrscheinlichkeit zum Glücklichen verschoben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chao-mines are said to be made in order to tilt probability toward fortunate occurrences and strange synchronicities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBChaoMines ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBProbabilityTiltedTowardFortuitous ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBProbabilityTiltedTowardFortuitous a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Probability tilted toward the fortuitous"@en, "Wahrscheinlichkeit zum Glücklichen verschoben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bending chance toward lucky events, strange synchronicities and the generally odd and marvellous."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBServitorProgrammingParadigm a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Servitor programming paradigm"@en, "Servitor-Programmierparadigma"@de ;
    skos:definition "The quasi-cybernetic approach began semi-seriously as Hine's 'User's Guide' styled as a computer manual but generated ideas, chiefly the analogy of the sigilised statement of intent to program code."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSigilCircuits a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sigil-circuits"@en, "Sigillen-Schaltkreise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chain the servitor's core sigil with enhancing symbols, e.g. rune Othel, the Kamea of Mars and rune Tir, closed by an infinity sign to keep the sequence looping; mixing systems seems to make no difference, and own elements can be created."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 118; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFlowchartServitorsIFTHEN a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Flowchart servitors (IF...THEN)"@en, "Flussdiagramm-Servitoren (WENN...DANN)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give a servitor conditions on which it acts (if a condition holds it switches on); build elaborate flowcharts in which controlling servitors direct subordinate servitors, each with its own job inside the larger programme."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 119; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBProgramViewVersusShotNudge a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Program view versus one-shot nudge"@en, "Programmsicht statt Einmal-Anstoß"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordinary results magic nudges one point of a situation in a mostly one-shot way; viewing situations as a program or flowchart lets many relevant elements be taken into account."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 120; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFunctionalSpiritsGrimoires a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Functional spirits of the grimoires"@en, "Funktionale Geister der Grimoires"@de ;
    skos:definition "Another approach to evocation works with spirits governing a situation, as in grimoires like the Lesser Key of Solomon, handbooks giving spirits' forms, names, sigils and conjurations; their names and forms are bizarre but their powers directly functional."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine ascribes this to a work he names and does not cite by edition: The Lesser Key of Solomon the King, as Hine names it, with the Keys of Solomon named beside it. The node holds what Condensed Chaos reports; the named work is reachable in its own right and is not read here, so the node is entered as Hine's ascription and not as a mediated reading of that work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 120; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRAUMNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Raum"@en, "Raum"@de ;
    skos:definition "A grimoire spirit said to show itself as a blackbird and to be able to cause love, make enemies friends, or ruin cities and good names."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "RAUM" ;
    pm:nameRole "Goetic spirit" ;
    skos:note "Hine ascribes this to a work he names and does not cite by edition: The Lesser Key of Solomon the King, as Hine names it, for the spirit Raum. The node holds what Condensed Chaos reports; the named work is reachable in its own right and is not read here, so the node is entered as Hine's ascription and not as a mediated reading of that work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBClassicalTriangleConjuration a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Classical triangle conjuration"@en, "Klassische Dreieckskonjuration"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the long-established ritual the spirits are summoned into a triangle and bound by ceremony to the magician's will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBGOFLOWOLFOGNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Goflowolfog"@en, "Goflowolfog"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spirit that eases traffic blockages; appears as a shades-wearing cat on a skateboard bringing a wind and a 'Neeowww' sound; cool, stylish, relaxed, speedy, graceful; pleased by giving others space to move and kindness to cats; sigil a circle with two opposite-running arrows. Assembled at a London seminar during a heat wave."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "GOFLOWOLFOG" ;
    pm:nameRole "functional spirit of traffic" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEasingTrafficStoppages a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Easing traffic stoppages"@en, "Verkehrsstaus lösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting stalled traffic moving again via a functional spirit; at least taking one's mind off stress."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSituationalSummoningGoflowolfog a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Situational summoning of Goflowolfog"@en, "Situatives Rufen von Goflowolfog"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stuck in a jam or a halted train, listen for the 'Neeowww' and watch for him shooting past with a breath of wind; catch his eye by becoming, inwardly at least, almost as cool as he; picture riding with him on the skateboard through the obstruction for a moment; then drop the picture and relax so that he can work. If things move even a few yards, pay him back: give someone else room to move (stand aside, let a car in) or treat the next cat one meets kindly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSummoningEasesJamOrStressYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Summoning eases jam or stress"@en, "Rufen lindert Stau oder Stress"@de ;
    skos:definition "The summoning is said to help traffic move, and if nothing else to distract from stress."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"if nothing else\")."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSituationalSummoningGoflowolfog ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEasingTrafficStoppages ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 121; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBPaymentAfterSpiritPerforms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Payment after the spirit performs"@en, "Gegenleistung nach Wirken des Geistes"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the spirit performs, you are beholden to offer something in return (good manners); the offering follows the result."@en ;
    skos:note "Read as a duty following the spirit's performance; entered as a concept because the offering has no node of its own apart from the summoning practice, which already names both forms of repayment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 122; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBDesigningFunctionalSpirit a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Designing a functional spirit"@en, "Einen funktionalen Geist entwerfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "1) Name the general situation (traffic). 2) Define its function there (easing stoppages). 3) Choose a name and make it 'barbaric', e.g. by mirroring (GO FLOW to GOFLOWOLFOG). 4) Choose a memorable, incongruous shape like grimoire spirits (cat on skateboard). 5) Define its disposition (cool, stylish) and how it responds to those who adopt its qualities. Use its sound as mantra and its sigil as talisman on vehicles or as evocation focus; build your own grimoires, ideally with friends."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 122; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBConfidenceMemeticSpreadSpirits a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence and memetic spread of spirits"@en, "Vertrauen und memetische Verbreitung von Geistern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The more successful usages are reported, the more confidence in the spirit rises; with time and wide use its image may enter the cultural meme-pool."@en ;
    skos:note "The text hedges this (\"may\")."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 122; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBTrapSpiritsOnlyRitualOurCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Trap: spirits only in ritual and in our heads"@en, "Falle: Geister nur im Ritual und im Kopf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians often slip into believing that gods, demons, allies and faeries are reachable only in formal magical settings, are there to serve us, and exist only in our minds."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondBReturnPantheistModelSpirits ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 123; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBehavioursBeliefsSpiritsMemes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Behaviours and beliefs as spirits (memes)"@en, "Verhaltensweisen und Überzeugungen als Geister (Meme)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine treats certain behaviours, attitudes and beliefs as spirits understood as memes: ideas that live apart from the people carrying them and spread through them like viruses."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 123; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAddictionNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Spirit of (heroin) addiction"@en, "Geist der (Heroin-)Sucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Addiction regarded as a spirit; Hine reports having kept the spirit of heroin addiction out of a few houses."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Addiction" ;
    pm:nameRole "memetic spirit" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 123; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBarringSpiritHouse a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Barring a spirit from a house"@en, "Einem Geist ein Haus verwehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine reports keeping the spirit of heroin addiction out of particular houses; the method is not given."@en ;
    skos:note "Method not described; recorded as reported operation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 123; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBTarotPacksSpiritCollections a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tarot packs as spirit collections"@en, "Tarotdecks als Geistersammlungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identical decks become subtly different; a new deck must be broken in; well-used packs can be seen as collections of spirits arising from interaction; if each card has a spirit, all copies share it and one may summon those spirits with one's own card."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 123; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondBSummoningCardSpirits a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Summoning card spirits"@en, "Kartengeister rufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take it that each tarot card carries a spirit, and use one's own copy to call the spirit shared by every copy of that card."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 123; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSpiritsNewElements a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirits of new elements"@en, "Geister der neuen Elemente"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against conditioning to the four classical elements, Hine asks what spirits arise from petrol, electricity and nuclear power and whether we can interact with them; left to the reader."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 124; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondBReturnPantheistModelSpirits a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Return to pantheist model of spirits"@en, "Rückkehr zum pantheistischen Geistermodell"@de ;
    skos:definition "The cybernetic approach is said to lead back to the classical pantheist view: spirits are everywhere and stand apart from us, yet they grow out of how we experience the world; deciding they are there gives them form and force, and once given they tend to stay, within the field of information we move through."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 6 Chaos Servitors, p. 124; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

#
# Chapter 7, Ego Magic
#

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCParamountReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paramount (Consensus) Reality as the field of identity work"@en, "Paramount- (Konsens-)Realität als Feld der Identitätsarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine holds that the everyday social reality of roles and masks, usually dismissed as mundane, is neglected by magicians, and that a strength of Chaos Magic is its identity work inside this consensus reality, whose structure he likens to fractals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 125; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBeliefShifting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief and attitude shifting (felt, not only intellectual)"@en, "Glaubens- und Haltungswechsel (gefühlt, nicht nur intellektuell)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to adopt different belief systems and change attitudes in emotion and physical action as well as in thought, embracing what one previously rejected and so widening what one holds possible; compared to Tantric practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 125; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDeterminationForBeliefShifting a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Great determination needed to enter another belief system"@en, "Große Entschlossenheit als Voraussetzung für den Eintritt in ein anderes Glaubenssystem"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine states that taking up a different belief system successfully requires great determination, because it means entering new social relations, masks, self-labels and their attendant emotions and behaviours."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDetermination ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBeliefShifting ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 125; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDetermination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Determination for belief-shifting and identity work"@en, "Entschlossenheit für Glaubenswechsel und Identitätsarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The drive, stamina and determination the text names as needed to enter a new belief system and to keep stripping away layers of identity; belief-shifting is said to take time and an investment of emotional energy as well."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 125, 129, 132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFragileIdentity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prolonged paradigm shifting reveals identity as fragile"@en, "Andauernder Paradigmenwechsel zeigt die Zerbrechlichkeit der Identität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Long practice of social paradigm shifting is said to bring home that identity is fragile; selfhood arises from internalised self-labels and alliances, often one set of social relations becoming the core label."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 125; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAlienNessElitism a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Sense of alien-ness can turn into ego-bound elitism"@en, "Gefühl der Fremdheit kann in ichgebundenen Elitismus umschlagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians frequently describe feeling increasingly estranged to consensus reality; Hine warns this perception can easily show itself as egotistic elitism or a standoffish manner, and how it is handled matters especially in Chaos and Tantric paradigms."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEgoToExo ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 126; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIdentityDeconstruction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chaos and Tantric paradigms deconstruct rather than reinforce identity"@en, "Chaos- und Tantra-Paradigma dekonstruieren statt Identität zu festigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In these paradigms the emphasis is on taking identity apart instead of strengthening attachment to one set of social relations, which would limit range of expression and movement."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 126; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMythicTime a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Entering a magical universe as imposing order and Mythic Time"@en, "Eintritt in ein magisches Universum als Ordnungsstiftung und mythische Zeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entering a magical universe is described as imposing order on chaos, entering Mythic or Eternal Time and gaining continuity and an anchored identity; Hine reads the magical revival as driven by a search for a past and by need for escape routes from Paramount Reality, and magical universes as promising a meta-theory."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 126-127; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEgoToExo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "From Ego to Exo: becoming a magician as continual change of identity"@en, "Vom Ego zum Exo: Magierwerdung als fortwährender Identitätswandel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Becoming a magician is said to imply continual modification of identity, moving between paradigms, learning skills and shedding outworn life-patterns, a shift from an Ego based on the self-other divide to an Exo, the self in continual dynamic engagement."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 127; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSelfLove a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-Love (Spare): fluid identity without need for validation"@en, "Selbstliebe (Spare): fließende Identität ohne Bestätigungsbedürfnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The point at which identity is continually deconstructed, fluidity of expression is reached and one no longer needs others to validate the self; not narcissism but a void at the core of identity able to enter any set of social relations without being trapped, granting wide liberty of movement and self-expression with no need to define oneself. Hine adds it need not mean withdrawal from consensus reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 127-128; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEscapeRoutes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Escape routes as dead ends; magic as the great escape route"@en, "Fluchtwege als Sackgassen; Magie als der große Fluchtweg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drugs, sex, fantasy, communes, separatism, therapies and romanticism are called escape routes that ultimately prove dead ends and support paramount reality, which recaptures such enclaves; magic is called the great escape route, whose maxim is that changing enough identity makes the structure follow, unlike politics which changes structure to change identity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 128; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFluidIdentityStress a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fluid identity is liberating but unsettling and stressful"@en, "Fließende Identität befreit, verunsichert aber und belastet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine notes that identity rendered fluid and open to will and imagination can liberate but is also deeply unsettling and stressful, provoking nostalgia, denial, cynicism and sensory screening."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEgoToExo ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 128; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCErisStupidBook a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "Eris epigraph from the Stupid Book"@en, "Eris-Motto aus dem Stupid Book"@de ;
    skos:definition "An epigraph is attributed to Eris: matter is her playground which she makes and breaks, inviting laughter."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Not stated; the words stand as an epigraph credited to Eris and to the Stupid Book, with no author named" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Eris" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Given as an epigraph between two paragraphs, with no account of how or by whom the words were obtained." ;
    skos:note "Hine ascribes this to a work he names and does not cite by edition: Eris, the Stupid Book, quoted as an epigraph in Hine, Condensed Chaos (New Falcon, 1995), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 129; no edition is given. The node holds what Condensed Chaos reports; the named work is reachable in its own right and is not read here, so the node is entered as Hine's ascription and not as a mediated reading of that work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCParamountRealityPlayground a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chaoist paradigm: Paramount Reality as playground, embraced not transcended"@en, "Chaoistisches Paradigma: Paramount-Realität als Spielplatz, umarmt statt überwunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Behind masks there may be nothing but a spinning void; the Chaoist paradigm grants freedom to be many individuals by embracing paramount reality joyfully, making it a playground for will and desire; from Self-Love one brings shards of the future to earth. Contrasted with most magical perspectives which seek to transcend it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDeterminationForStrippingIdentity a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Drive, stamina and determination for continual stripping of identity"@en, "Antrieb, Ausdauer und Entschlossenheit für das fortwährende Abtragen von Identität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine calls the continual stripping away of identity layers the activity of an elite, since few have the needed drive, stamina and determination."@en ;
    skos:note "The text states the requirement as a quality few possess and names no consequence of lacking it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDetermination ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSelfLove ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 129; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Deconditioning process"@en, "Dekonditionierungsprozess"@de ;
    skos:definition "Continual self-awareness work: discover what you consist of in acquired beliefs, attitudes and behaviour patterns, and chip away at limiting ones; never finished because new limitations form, often unconsciously."@en ;
    skos:note "In Tantra the discarding of a set of limitations is called Klesha-smashing (p. 130); chapter 9 gives the same name to work with personal demons, pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPersonalDemons."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 130-132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioningYieldsSelfAwareness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Deconditioning yields awareness of one's conditioning"@en, "Dekonditionierung bewirkt Gewahrsein der eigenen Konditionierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The deconditioning process is called essentially one of self-awareness, discovering who one is in terms of acquired beliefs, attitudes and patterns."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSelfAwareness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSelfAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-awareness of one's conditioning"@en, "Selbstgewahrsein der eigenen Konditionierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing what one consists of in acquired beliefs, attitudes and behaviour patterns, and being able to loosen them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCImprintSusceptibility a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical beliefs easy to reprogram; deeper structures resist and hide"@en, "Magische Überzeugungen leicht umzuprogrammieren; tiefere Strukturen widerstehen und verbergen sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reprogramming magical beliefs is said to be relatively easy, but some levels of belief resist conscious change, partly by staying invisible to awareness; beliefs are often nested and rooted in formative experiences (Leary's imprint susceptibility), and Leary's 8-circuit metaprogramming model can aid deconditioning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCTacNukeGnosis a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gnosis as tac-nuke against belief structures"@en, "Gnosis als taktische Atombombe gegen Glaubensstrukturen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Now and then turning to a strong form of gnosis, sexual ecstasy, an overload of pain or LSD (called Hofmann's elixir), as a tactical nuke that brings down whole towers in the city of belief, alongside the steady chipping away of deconditioning."@en ;
    skos:note "The routes into gnosis themselves are treated in earlier chapters of the book, outside this section."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioningNotIntellectual a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Deconditioning is not merely intellectual"@en, "Dekonditionierung ist nicht bloß intellektuell"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accepting a rejected belief intellectually is easy; acting from the new position and risking emotional upheaval takes more resilience."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 130; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIntellectualLiberationFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intellectual acceptance mistaken for liberation (young magician)"@en, "Intellektuelle Annahme mit Befreiung verwechselt (junger Magier)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A young male magician accepted his repressed homoerotic attraction intellectually, then had encounters that gave him no physical pleasure but only bolstered his conviction of being liberated; Hine calls this an easy trap."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: intellectual acceptance of a rejected desire, followed by acts that give no felt pleasure and only feed the belief of being freed. No deadline or rate; the failure is put on the operator. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMagicianGuiltScript a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "\"As a magician I ought to feel no guilt\" is another ego-identification"@en, "„Als Magier dürfte ich keine Schuld fühlen“ ist nur eine weitere Ich-Identifikation"@de ;
    skos:definition "The common inner script that a magician ought to manage anything free of guilt or unease is itself an ego-identification and breeds intrapsychic contradictions."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDesireToOvercomeFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Restructuring fails unless desire to overcome outweighs desire to keep"@en, "Umstrukturierung scheitert, wenn der Wunsch zu bewahren überwiegt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Habit and belief restructuring is said to succeed only if wanting to overcome a limitation outweighs wanting to keep it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the restructuring of a habit or belief does not take while the wish to keep the limitation outweighs the wish to overcome it. No deadline; the failure is put on the operator. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFanaticalShiftFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Surface belief change keeps the deep pattern (fanatic to fanatic)"@en, "Oberflächlicher Glaubenswechsel bewahrt das Tiefenmuster (Fanatiker zu Fanatiker)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shifting from fanatical Christian to fanatical magician alters only the outer beliefs; the underlying habit of shoring up identity by rejecting what does not fit remains."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: only the surface beliefs change, while the pattern of defending identity by rejecting what does not fit persists. No deadline; the failure is put on the operator. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCorePatternsUnpicked a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Unpicking core patterns is necessary for deconditioning"@en, "Auflösen der Kernmuster ist für Dekonditionierung notwendig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deconditioning is said to necessitate unpicking the core threads of self-image and understanding how one has conditioned oneself."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSelfAwareness ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Only the surface beliefs shift, and the deep habit of shoring up identity by rejecting whatever does not fit the self-image stays in place, as when a fanatical Christian becomes a fanatical magician." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAmoralityEgoConquestDeception a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Declared amorality and conquered Ego are self-deceptions"@en, "Erklärte Amoralität und besiegtes Ego sind Selbsttäuschungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trying to throw off all conditioning at once and declaring oneself amoral is often self-deception; claims to have conquered the Ego are fiction, since without a strong identity one cannot act, and magic is about doing."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 131; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAdoptingNewMasks a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Adopting new masks"@en, "Annehmen neuer Masken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adopt beliefs, attitudes and self-identifications lying well beyond your dominant self-image: change political ideas, switch introvert to extrovert, shed and adopt habits, vary sexual behaviour, adopt new gestures and postures, become passionate about things you think trivial, move through subcultures; wear the mask continually in social relations, not only in your head."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 131-132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBeliefShiftingTakesTime a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Belief shifting takes time, emotional energy and determination"@en, "Glaubenswechsel braucht Zeit, emotionale Energie und Entschlossenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "You cannot decide overnight to be a hedonistic Satanist; belief shifting needs time and investment of emotion and determination, and doing it only in one's head is too easy."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAdoptingNewMasks ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCNewIdentityAcceptedSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others believe in your new identity"@en, "Andere sind von der neuen Identität überzeugt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treat it as success when others believe in your new identity and accept or reject you because of it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: other people are convinced by the new identity and accept or reject the operator on that basis. No deadline; the sign shows in the behaviour of others, though the operator judges it. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAdoptingNewMasks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEmpathy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Empathy with other world-views"@en, "Empathie für andere Weltsichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Belief shifting is said to yield empathy, the capacity to grasp how someone else sees the world, and the freeing realisation that one's own beliefs are as nonsensical as those once opposed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMasksYieldEmpathy a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mask-wearing yields empathy"@en, "Maskentragen bewirkt Empathie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Belief shifting by adopting masks produces empathy and relativising insight into one's own beliefs."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAdoptingNewMasks ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEmpathy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCShatteringBeliefStructures a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shattering of belief-structure layers"@en, "Zerschlagung von Schichten der Glaubensstruktur"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intense gnosis is said to break apart strata of belief."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCTacNukeYieldsShattering a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Intense gnosis yields shattering of belief layers"@en, "Intensive Gnosis bewirkt Zerschlagung von Glaubensschichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gnosis used as a tac-nuke breaks apart strata of belief, though transiently without follow-up."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCTacNukeGnosis ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCShatteringBeliefStructures ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 130, 132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGrowingBackFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shattered belief structures grow back without follow-up"@en, "Zerschlagene Glaubensstrukturen wachsen ohne Nacharbeit nach"@de ;
    skos:definition "People reporting Illumination often claim all repressive structures fell away, but a torn-down building grows back, sometimes in another shape; the shattering by intense gnosis is generally transitory without subsequent work."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the felt shattering of belief structures fades and the structures grow back, sometimes in another shape, when no further work follows. No deadline, though the effect is called transitory; the failure is put on the operator who omits the follow-up. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCTacNukeGnosis."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDiceManCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Consider effects of deconditioning on others"@en, "Wirkung der Dekonditionierung auf andere bedenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine advises considering the effects of the process on other people, pointing to Rhinehart's The Dice Man."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 132; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMagusItis a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Magus-itis: the ego defends itself with a sense of superiority"@en, "Magus-itis: das Ego verteidigt sich mit Überlegenheitsgefühl"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ego resists becoming more adaptive; a subtle defence is the suspicion, which can become an obsession, of being better than everyone, leading some to declare themselves Maguses, Witch Queens, avatars or Masters."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 132-133; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCHumanCattleFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Calling others \"the herd\" signals going astray"@en, "Andere „Herde“ zu nennen zeigt Abirren an"@de ;
    skos:definition "If you catch yourself calling everyone else the herd or human cattle, it is time to re-examine where you are going."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: catching oneself calling everyone else the herd or human cattle shows that the ego's defence of superiority has taken hold. No deadline; the failure is put on the operator. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCNothingIsTrueConflict a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Acting wholly on Hassan i Sabbah's maxim brings conflict"@en, "Volles Handeln nach „Nichts ist wahr, alles ist erlaubt“ führt zu Konflikten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting totally from Hassan i Sabbah's maxim is likely to bring conflict with people and authorities who hold fixed views of what is not permitted; hence chaoists are seldom wholly without morals."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDeconditioning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMoralityFromWithin a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Morality grows from within"@en, "Moral wächst von innen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A basic axiom of magical philosophy, per Hine: morality arises inwardly once one can tell apart beliefs one was taught from beliefs one wills."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCChartingTheSelf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Charting the Self: seven self-examination exercises"@en, "Das Selbst kartieren: sieben Übungen zur Selbsterforschung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's set of preliminary self-examination exercises, in this order: Third Person, Lists, A Book of Blunders, Suppressions, Conversations, Destroying the Stereotype, Storytelling."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 133-134; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCChartingYieldsSelfAwareness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-examination exercises yield self-awareness"@en, "Übungen der Selbsterforschung bewirken Selbstgewahrsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercises of Charting the Self and the recognition of habitual patterns are given as steps towards self-awareness, identifying patterns one holds onto without seeing that they no longer serve."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCThirdPerson, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCStrengthsWeaknessesLists, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBookOfBlunders, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSuppressions, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCInternalConversations, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDestroyingTheStereotype, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCStorytelling, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCPatternRecognition ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSelfAwareness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 133-134; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCHonestyBeforeSelfExamination a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Honesty not to flinch from unpalatable parts of oneself"@en, "Ehrlichkeit, vor unangenehmen Seiten nicht zurückzuschrecken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The self-examination exercises are said to need only the honesty to face, without recoiling, the parts of oneself one dislikes."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCUnflinchingHonesty ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCChartingTheSelf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCUnflinchingHonesty a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Honesty that does not flinch from oneself"@en, "Ehrlichkeit, die vor sich selbst nicht zurückweicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The honesty to face, without recoiling, the parts of oneself one finds unpalatable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCThirdPerson a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Third Person account"@en, "Bericht in der dritten Person"@de ;
    skos:definition "Write an account of yourself in the third person as if by someone else, discussing strengths and weaknesses like a work reference."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCStrengthsWeaknessesLists a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Lists of strengths and weaknesses"@en, "Listen von Stärken und Schwächen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Divide a page in two and list strengths and weaknesses; extend to life successes and failures, fears and fantasies, things that attract and repel you."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 133; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBookOfBlunders a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "A Book of Blunders"@en, "Ein Buch der Fehlgriffe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fill a blank book with every life episode you found emotionally painful, guilty or embarrassing, neither rising above nor wallowing, to get an honest catalogue of negative past events."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 133-134; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSuppressions a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Suppressions list"@en, "Liste der Unterdrückungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "List the parts of yourself you try to keep down, such as fears, fantasies, desires and crazy thoughts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCInternalConversations a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Identifying internal conversations"@en, "Innere Gespräche erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identify the inner stories you tell yourself about what you can and cannot do, and how you uphold them, as a step to self-awareness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDestroyingTheStereotype a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Destroying the Stereotype"@en, "Das Stereotyp zerstören"@de ;
    skos:definition "When someone provokes you to label them as a stereotype, quickly fire alternative explanations at yourself for why they look as they do; note how many other identifications you can generate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCStorytelling a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Storytelling about strangers"@en, "Geschichten über Fremde erfinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Watch people talking in a room and invent as many stories about them as you can."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCPatternRecognition a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pattern recognition in relationships"@en, "Mustererkennung in Beziehungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identify habituated patterns of thought and behaviour, especially those carried from one relationship to the next which are no longer viable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 134; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCObsessionalDemons a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Obsessional demons: obsessions as old programs"@en, "Obsessive Dämonen: Obsessionen als alte Programme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Obsessions are described as mental monsters we breed ourselves, programs written in childhood from critical moments, which seize us when a gap opens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 135; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDefenseMechanisms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Defense mechanisms against conflicting desires"@en, "Abwehrmechanismen gegen widerstreitende Wünsche"@de ;
    skos:definition "The more value placed on an emotional pattern, the more ambiguous signals are read as supporting it; conflict between desire and mental constructs is handled by aggression, apathy, regression, sublimation or intellectualisation, which are normal until they become an obsessive automatic loop."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 135-136; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSublimationCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Sublimated demons return by the back door"@en, "Sublimierte Dämonen kehren durch die Hintertür zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Redirecting energy into acceptable form does not get rid of demons; they come round the back and wait until the mind is left open."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDefenseMechanisms ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 135; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFantasyObsession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fantasy as cornerstone of obsession"@en, "Phantasie als Grundstein der Obsession"@de ;
    skos:definition "Starter, maintainer and stopper fantasies; a fantasy is torn between fulfilling and preserving it, producing a closed loop driven by dread of failing and lust of result, which clouds reason and impairs action. In occult terms this is a thought-form fed by psychic energy; everyone has personal Tunnels of Set."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 136-137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSeeingTheProgram a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing that an obsession is a program"@en, "Erkennen, dass eine Obsession ein Programm ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognising, by a sudden insight or through a friend's gentle remarks, that one is acting out a program, and owning the obsession as one's own creature without taking it for the whole self."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSeeingTheProgramFirst a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "First recognise that a program is running"@en, "Zuerst erkennen, dass es ein Programm gibt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before the obsession can be dismantled one must first recognise that a program is running and own it as one's creature without identifying wholly with it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSeeingTheProgram ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCHuntingTheObsession ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCHuntingTheObsession a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Hunting the obsession"@en, "Die Obsession jagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turn from prey to hunter: pull the obsession apart, name its parts, search memory for its scaffolding, shrink and devour it layer by layer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCHuntingYieldsFreedom a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Hunting the obsession yields freedom and effectiveness"@en, "Jagd auf die Obsession bewirkt Freiheit und Wirksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dismantling the obsession may leave the practitioner freer and more effective."@en ;
    skos:note "The three remedies for the components of obsession are entered as further practices of this claim, since the text names the freeing as the outcome of the whole unbinding."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCHuntingTheObsession, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCCognitiveCutDown, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCPhysiologicalStilling, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBehavioralComponent ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFreedomFromObsession ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFreedomFromObsession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from obsession, more effective action"@en, "Freiheit von Obsession, wirksameres Handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unbinding one's knots is said to equal any sorcery in power and may leave one freer, more effective in action and less prone to repeating past errors."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCObsessionComponents a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three components of obsession with matching remedies"@en, "Drei Komponenten der Obsession mit zugehörigen Mitteln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine divides the grip of obsession into cognitive, physiological and behavioural components, each with its own countermeasure."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCCognitiveCutDown a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cognitive: cut down obsessive thoughts"@en, "Kognitiv: obsessive Gedanken zurückschneiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ruthlessly analyse your thoughts and feelings about the situation and pare them back through self-assessment, banishing or the like."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCPhysiologicalStilling a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Physiological: still the body"@en, "Physiologisch: den Körper beruhigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calm the anxious body (pulse, muscular tension, blood pressure) by relaxation and meditation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBehavioralComponent a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Behavioural: others and divination reveal obsessive behaviour"@en, "Verhalten: andere und Divination zeigen obsessives Verhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Obsessive behaviour is often inappropriate and harmful to others and usually needs others to point it out; I Ching or Tarot may help analyse it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 137; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBreakingBounds a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking Bounds: positive against negative ego-identification"@en, "Grenzen brechen: positive gegen negative Ich-Identifikation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Set a positive ego-identification against a negative one so that, in a situation bringing them into conflict, the stronger positive one weakens the negative; Hine stresses it is more becoming aware of the transaction than a deliberate contest."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 137-138; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBreakingBoundsMathematics a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Hine's mathematics block weakened by computer identity"@en, "Hines Mathematikblockade durch Computer-Identität geschwächt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine reports a long-held mathematics block; building databases needing tax and discount formulas brought it into conflict with his identity as one who makes computers obey, and the latter won, weakening his resistance to maths."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBreakingBounds ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCWeakenedBlock ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 137-138; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCWeakenedBlock a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Weakening a conditioned block"@en, "Schwächung einer konditionierten Blockade"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reduced resistance to an area one was conditioned to avoid."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 138; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSexualIdentityConflict a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sexual identity assumption as conflict of ego-identifications"@en, "Annahme sexueller Identität als Konflikt von Ich-Identifikationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assuming a negatively conditioned sexual identity shows the same conflict between perceived nature, negative conditioning and the wish to act, joining desire with self-loathing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 138; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCLegionOfSelves a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Legion of Selves"@en, "Legion der Selbste"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of higher and lower selves, the self is a multiplicity of identities from which self-identity emerges; compared to the Tantric image of Shiva amid a bag of Shaktis."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 138; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCManySelves a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Many Selves: rotating the seat of identity"@en, "Viele Selbste: den Sitz der Identität wechseln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identify your different selves and give each, as circumstances fit, a turn as the seat of identity; define several distinct personalities to switch into and out of at need."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 138; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCManySelvesYieldFlipping a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Defining several selves allows flipping between them"@en, "Mehrere Selbste zu bestimmen erlaubt den Wechsel zwischen ihnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identifying one's selves and defining distinct personalities, such as the Neutral Self, lets one move in and out of them as the need arises."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCManySelves, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNeutralSelf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPersonalityFlipping ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 138-139; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPersonalityFlipping a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Switching between defined personalities at need"@en, "Bedarfsweiser Wechsel zwischen definierten Persönlichkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being able to flip in and out of distinct personalities as situations require."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 138; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNeutralSelf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Neutral Self persona"@en, "Die Persona des Neutralen Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sample personality: hold yourself slightly aloof to observe others covertly for strengths and weaknesses, move economically, measure every word, show neither approval nor disapproval, accept others' behaviour as given."@en ;
    skos:note "Given as a defined self to flip into."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 139; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFictionalEntitiesDefence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Defence of working with fictional and non-historical entities"@en, "Verteidigung der Arbeit mit fiktiven, nicht-historischen Wesenheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine argues against critics who say magic needs historical or mythological roots, inner-plane contacts or traditions, and who object to Cthulhu Mythos, Rocky Horror on the Tree of Life or newly channelled gods."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the critics are unnamed and stand in the text only as he reports their objections."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 139; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAnyBeliefSystem a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Any belief system works if it excites you"@en, "Jedes Glaubenssystem wirkt, solange es einen begeistert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magic requires a belief system as the symbolic and linguistic frame for interpreting experience, but which one is irrelevant if it excites you; most magicians develop personal systems, e.g. Spare's Alphabet of Desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 139; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCVeracityOfBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Veracity of belief as key to success; plausible rationale buffers belief"@en, "Glaubwürdigkeit als Erfolgsschlüssel; plausible Begründung stützt den Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "If you can devise a plausible explanation of how something should work, pseudoscientific or qabalistic, it most likely will, since the rationale buffers belief; Hine finds total certainty makes success more likely and can be transmitted to others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 139-140; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCChakraBeliefShift a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief-shift experiment with chakra systems"@en, "Glaubenswechsel-Experiment mit Chakrensystemen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meditate on the seven chakras and drill their symbolism until seven-chakra experiences arise; then switch to the five centres of Regardie's Middle Pillar and observe corresponding results."@en ;
    skos:note "Offered as an experiment in belief-shifting, pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBeliefShifting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSystemExperiencesSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Experiences matching the adopted system"@en, "Erfahrungen gemäß dem angenommenen System"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced result: you will have seven-chakra experiences, and then results accordant with the Middle Pillar model."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: experiences shaped like whatever system one has drilled into oneself, first seven-chakra experiences and then results matching the Middle Pillar. No deadline; the sign is announced in advance and follows the system chosen. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCChakraBeliefShift."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCUninvestedBeliefFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lack of belief invested in the system"@en, "Mangelnder in das System investierter Glaube"@de ;
    skos:definition "Implied failure condition: a belief system serves magic only so long as belief can be invested in it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a belief system gives no results unless belief can be invested in it; stated only as the positive condition. No deadline; the failure is put on the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 140; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBeliefSystemMatrix a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief system as matrix for emotional energy; pop myths as modern mythology"@en, "Glaubenssystem als Matrix für emotionale Energie; Popmythen als moderne Mythologie"@de ;
    skos:definition "A belief system is a matrix into which emotion is poured, as when a film becomes real for a moment; Star Trek mirrors our psychology as modern myth with characters embodying qualities and internally consistent rules."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, pp. 140-141; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRolePlayingMythos a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Role-playing game to enter a mythic universe"@en, "Rollenspiel zum Eintritt in ein mythisches Universum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Increase participation in a fictional mythos by group role-play, generating its semblance for a few hours, supported by books, comics, videos and supplements."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSpockInvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Invoking Mr Spock for an exam"@en, "Mr. Spock für eine Prüfung invozieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "A colleague facing a computer exam chose Spock as god-form, learned all about him and went around repeating his catchphrase until thoroughly Spock-ified."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGodFormConcentration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mental concentration for programming via god-form"@en, "Geistige Konzentration fürs Programmieren durch Gottesform"@de ;
    skos:definition "Concentration of mind on a task by assuming a fitting god-form."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSpockNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Mr Spock"@en, "Mr. Spock"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treated as the most powerful mythic figure for dealing with computers; logical."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Mr. Spock" ;
    pm:nameRole "god-form (fictional) of logic and computing" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSpockInvocationYieldsExamResult a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spock invocation yields better exam result"@en, "Spock-Invokation bewirkt besseres Prüfungsergebnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The colleague scored higher than he otherwise expected."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSpockInvocation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGodFormConcentration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGreatOldOnesNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Great Old Ones (Cthulhu Mythos)"@en, "Die Großen Alten (Cthulhu-Mythos)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held to stand outside most human mythologies, akin to Norse giants and pre-Olympian Titans, shadowy and only partly glimpsable, too chaotic for orthodox systems, primal; fear of the unknown (after Lovecraft) the strongest emotion attached to them."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Great Old Ones", "Cthulhu" ;
    pm:nameRole "primal chaotic beings from fiction worked with magically" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNarniaMythicSystem a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Working a mythic system from fiction (Narnia)"@en, "Arbeit mit einem fiktionalen Mythensystem (Narnia)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine reports interesting results from working a mythic system built on the Narnia books of C. S. Lewis."@en ;
    skos:note "Results not specified."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 141; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMetaprogramming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Metaprogramming: adopt a belief briefly then drop it"@en, "Metaprogrammierung: Glauben kurz annehmen und wieder ablegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A belief can be held for a short time and then dropped."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 142; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCActingAsIfGodsReal a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Behaving as if gods are real during ritual"@en, "Im Ritual so handeln, als seien Götter real"@de ;
    skos:definition "In ritual act as if the gods are real whatever your theory; in a Cthulhu ritual, adopt the belief that a mistake will get you slimed, to build tension; drop the belief outside the ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 142; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRitualTension a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual tension built by adopted belief"@en, "Rituelle Spannung durch angenommenen Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The necessary emotional tension in a ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 142; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSuspensionOfDisbelief a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Suspension of Disbelief with a despised author"@en, "Aussetzen des Unglaubens an einem verachteten Autor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take a book expounding an idea you consider rubbish and try to grasp what its author means without your inner voice abusing the page."@en ;
    skos:note "Offered as a form of belief-shifting, pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBeliefShifting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 142; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCNaggingDisbelief a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Nagging doubt that magic does not work"@en, "Nagender Zweifel, dass Magie nicht wirkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "For fledgling magicians the hardest suspension is the nagging doubt that it all does not work; talk and reading do not remove it, only experience does: one act showing magic works outweighs a thousand arguments."@en ;
    skos:note "Recorded at first as a condition of failure; the text gives the doubt as an obstacle for beginners, not as a sign that a working failed, and it is entered as a caution."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSuspensionOfDisbelief ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 142; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIntensityOfBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intensity of belief makes any system work"@en, "Glaubensintensität lässt jedes System wirken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whether historical, esoteric or fictional, a system works through intensity of belief; what counts is being emotionally moved by it or using it as a vehicle of will. Use whatever works for you."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 7 Ego Magic, p. 142; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .


#
# Chapter 8, Kali in the Disco
#

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCKaliPathworking a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Kali pathworking for power of attraction"@en, "Kali-Pfadarbeit für Anziehungskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "A friend wanting more attraction for women chose Kali; with Hine she worked out a pathworking in which she merged with a modern Kali image and strode into the women's disco, the crowd awestruck by her poise."@en ;
    skos:note "No outcome of the working is stated beyond the scene imagined; its benefit is referred to as obvious at the start of the next section."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCKaliNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Kali"@en, "Kali"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hindu goddess of death and sex, chosen as the figure to boost attraction; her pyre is the setting of an initiatory dismemberment."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Kali" ;
    pm:nameRole "goddess of sex and death; invoked for power of attraction; initiator through dismemberment" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 143; ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 184; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation defined: identification with a mythic figure to access its qualities"@en, "Invokation definiert: Identifikation mit einer mythischen Gestalt zum Zugang zu ihren Eigenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gods and goddesses are personifications of physical and mental attributes we can engender in ourselves; invocation is temporarily identifying with a mythic figure so far that we gain access to its abilities, like adolescents modelling a culture hero. It is a case of controlled feedback reinforcing the belief one is becoming something other than one's dominant self-perception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 143-144; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocationSkills a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Skills that invocation draws on"@en, "Fertigkeiten, auf die Invokation zurückgreift"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some skill in visualising and in using the voice, awareness of how posture and gesture are used, kinesthetic memory, practice in entering gnosis by its several routes, relaxation, and awareness of oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocationSkillsRequired a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Skills needed to get the best from invocation"@en, "Fertigkeiten für bestmögliche Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocation at its best needs some ability in visualisation, voice, posture and gesture, kinesthetic memory, routes into gnosis, relaxation and awareness of self; performing invocations also develops these skills."@en ;
    skos:note "The same passage calls the doing of invocations a very practical means of developing these skills; that claim is pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionYieldsInvocationSkills."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocationSkills ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionOfGodForms ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionYieldsInvocationSkills a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Performing invocations develops the skills they need"@en, "Invokationen auszuführen entwickelt die Fertigkeiten, die sie brauchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doing invocations is called a very practical means of building up the skills on which invocation itself depends."@en ;
    skos:note "The passage speaks of invocation in general; the god-form assumption is the invocation technique the chapter gives."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionOfGodForms ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocationSkills ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPoiseAndAttraction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enhanced attractiveness, confidence and poise"@en, "Gesteigerte Anziehungskraft, Selbstvertrauen und Haltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Raising confidence and poise through identification with an outsized mythic figure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCKaliPathworkingYieldsPoise a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The Kali working boosts confidence and poise"@en, "Die Kali-Arbeit stärkt Selbstvertrauen und Haltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The benefit of raising confidence and poise through identification with a figure larger than life is said to be obvious from the anecdote of the friend who merged with Kali."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCKaliPathworking ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPoiseAndAttraction ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 143; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocationUses a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Uses of invocation"@en, "Anwendungen der Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocation can make a shadow-self more prominent by bringing it fully to awareness; give insight into a little-known entity; boost capacity for other magic, e.g. sorcery after invoking a fitting entity leaves one charged with power and supernormally single-minded; obtain information by invoking an oracular deity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 143-144; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRaHoorKhuitNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Ra-Hoor-Khuit"@en, "Ra-Hoor-Khuit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Egyptian deity, aspect of hawk-headed Horus, significant in Thelema; god of strength and silence, appearing as hawk or hawk-headed man, martial, with solar associations; the Aeon card of the Thoth deck represents him. Invoking him means identifying with power, confidence, poise, hawk-like perceptual acuity and detachment from the target of will."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Ra-Hoor-Khuit (Ra-Hoor Khuit)" ;
    pm:nameRole "warrior god invoked for power and vision; lord of the Aeon" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 144; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRaHoorKhuitPathworking a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ra-Hoor-Khuit Pathworking"@en, "Ra-Hoor-Khuit-Pfadarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "After relaxation, in a relaxed attentive position, ideally from a tape: drift on the Nile with Thoth as guide to a pyramid; pass the sphinx reflecting on to know, will, dare, keep silent; climb to the Khephra archway veiled in purple and silver; descend a starlit passage; pass the scales of judgement, pick up a black feather; enter a starry temple with brass double-cube altar, green cross, red rose and green throne; repeat the god's name until golden radiance fills you; Ra-Hoor-Khuit appears, speaks and streams energy into your heart; see what you might accomplish; a star hangs above the altar; thank him with the feather and return."@en ;
    skos:note "Khephra, the scarab carrying the sun through the darkness, and Thoth as guide are figures of the script and are not entered as names of their own. The speech Ra-Hoor-Khuit gives in the script echoes the Book of the Law, which Hine does not cite."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 144-147; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFeelOfTheGod a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feel for a deity's qualities"@en, "Gespür für die Eigenschaften einer Gottheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pathworking is said to let you sense the qualities and moods linked with Ra-Hoor-Khuit, attuning to the ambiance for invoking him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 147; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPathworkingYieldsFeel a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Pathworking yields attunement to the god"@en, "Pfadarbeit bewirkt Einstimmung auf den Gott"@de ;
    skos:definition "Performing the Ra-Hoor-Khuit pathworking gives the feel of the god's qualities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRaHoorKhuitPathworking ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFeelOfTheGod ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 147; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPathworkingBeforeAssumption a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Pathworking before drawing the god into oneself"@en, "Pfadarbeit vor dem Hineinziehen des Gottes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pathworking is a first step; after experiencing the power so, one next draws it into oneself by assuming the god-form."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRaHoorKhuitPathworking ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionOfGodForms ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 147; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCStatementOfIntent a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Statement of intent for invocation"@en, "Absichtserklärung für die Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Determine and clearly state your intent, e.g. declaring one's will to call Ra-Hoor-Khuit to gain magical power and sight of one's next step."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 147; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionOfGodForms a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Assumption of God-Forms"@en, "Annahme von Gottesformen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stand in a posture of relaxed readiness; visualise the god behind you; breathe slowly, letting the pathworking sensations well up; feel his gaze and presence until the pressure is unbearable; then imagine him stepping forward into your body, arms stretched out, letting your outline become his and his power yours; repeat his speech; while charged, review your magical work and decide what to do next."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 147-148; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGodFormCharge a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Supercharged confidence and clarity of next step"@en, "Aufgeladenes Selbstvertrauen und Klarheit über den nächsten Schritt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feeling filled with energy yet calm and detached, full of confidence and power, and able to decide firmly what to do next."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 148; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionYieldsCharge a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "God-form assumption yields charged confidence"@en, "Gottesformannahme bewirkt aufgeladenes Selbstvertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assuming the god-form produces feeling charged with power and confidence while deciding next steps."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionOfGodForms ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGodFormCharge ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 148; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCEarthingInvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Earthing after invocation"@en, "Erdung nach der Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Briefly thank the god and visualise parting from him, e.g. he turns into a hawk and flies sunward bearing your will's seed into the future; then banish and go forth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 148; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAccomplishmentSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Charged confidence then peaceful sense of accomplishment"@en, "Aufgeladene Zuversicht, danach friedliches Erfolgsgefühl"@de ;
    skos:definition "First one should feel full of confidence and power; on earthing, this gives way to calm and the sense of having accomplished one's aim."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a charged, confident state while the god-form is held, then calm and a sense of having achieved the purpose after earthing. No deadline; felt only from within. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionOfGodForms and pmp:ChaosMagicCondCEarthingInvocation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 148; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocationAsDrama a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation as performance for the entity"@en, "Invokation als Aufführung für die Wesenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ritual invocation can be thought of as a performance for the entity: a good performance is rewarded, a poor one is not asked back; Hine studies actors and comedians for posture, gesture and voice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 148; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBlownLinesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Poor performance goes unrewarded"@en, "Schlechte Aufführung bleibt unbelohnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "If you blow your lines in the invocation-as-performance, the entity will not have you back."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: an invocation performed badly, likened to an actor who blows his lines, is not rewarded and the entity does not have the operator back. No deadline; the failure is put on the operator's performance. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionOfGodForms."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 148; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCThreePartInvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Three-part structure of a classical invocation"@en, "Dreiteiliger Aufbau einer klassischen Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "First recount the entity's deeds and history in the third person, then its qualities in the second person, then its powers in the first person so you gradually identify with it (illustrated with the big bad wolf)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 148-149; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRhythmAndDelivery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rhythm and delivery in invocation"@en, "Rhythmus und Vortrag in der Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rhythm carries consciousness, starts movement without effort and frees attention; invocatory delivery is more deliberate and projects emotion; the Deep Mind speaks in verse, and possessed speech worldwide shows rising-falling phrase ends with pauses, in English iambic pentameter; sound rhythms drive trance (EEG)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 149-150; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRhythmCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Rhythms can be devastating when caught off guard"@en, "Rhythmen können verheerend wirken, wenn man unvorbereitet ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trance-inducing sound rhythms, from lunar lapping to Pan's frenzy, can have devastating effect if one is caught off guard and susceptible."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRhythmAndDelivery ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 150; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCVerbalInvocationDesign a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Designing a verbal invocation by rhythm and delivery"@en, "Gestaltung einer verbalen Invokation nach Rhythmus und Vortrag"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consider how the god's qualities should sound in your voice, e.g. strong martial repetitive rhythm, calm and confident with gathering power for Ra-Hoor-Khuit; speak confidently from the heart rather than half-remembered book lines; book reading hampers gesture."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 150; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPostureAndGesture a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Postures and gestures associated with emotions reinforce invocation"@en, "Haltungen und Gesten verstärken die Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "A key invocatory skill is linking postures and gestures to fitting emotions and sensations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 150; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNeutralPosture a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Neutral Posture"@en, "Die neutrale Haltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Find a seated and also a standing posture of calm readiness, relaxed, attentive, prepared but not tense (not lying down), representing your Axis Mundi; move out of and back into it to demarcate magical acts, e.g. before and after a god-form."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 150-151; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocationPostures a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Posture changes during invocation; classical opening and closing postures"@en, "Haltungsänderung bei Invokation; klassische Öffnungs- und Schließhaltungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entities have characteristic postures or one can be decided in advance; as perception changes the body shifts, confidence drawing shoulders back and head up; feet apart and arms spread up and out is the classical invoking posture (extending and exposing body space), arms folded and head bowed the classical closing posture."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 151; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCGestureBattery a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Developing a battery of magical gestures"@en, "Entwicklung eines Repertoires magischer Gesten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Experiment until you have gestures expressing relaxation, drawing in, projecting power, etc.; the commonest modern gesture is jabbing the dominant hand out from the shoulder to project will into the future."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 152; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCClapEnchantment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Clap-and-fling enchantment"@en, "Klatsch-und-Wurf-Verzauberung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cup the hands, focus awareness until tingling and slight resistance are felt, imagine a ball of energy with a sigil forming in it, breathe deeply, clap loudly and fling outwards: a very simple enchantment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 152; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCHandTinglingSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tingling and resistance between the hands"@en, "Kribbeln und Widerstand zwischen den Händen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feeling a faint tingle and slight resistance when bringing the hands together indicates gathered power."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a faint tingling and slight resistance between the cupped hands. Given as part of the instruction and felt only from within; it says nothing of whether the enchantment comes about. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCClapEnchantment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 152; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCClapYieldsEnchantment a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The clap and fling casts an enchantment"@en, "Klatschen und Wegschleudern wirkt eine Verzauberung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clapping over the imagined ball of energy with its sigil and flinging it outwards is called a very simple means of casting an enchantment."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCClapEnchantment ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEnchantmentCasting ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 152; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEnchantmentCasting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Casting an enchantment"@en, "Wirken einer Verzauberung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sending a sigil-charged intention out as a spell."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 152; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMaskPersonality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Masks as magical objects with own personality"@en, "Masken als magische Objekte mit eigener Persönlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In shamanic cultures masks are powerful weapons (locked away, downcast eyes); a mask has its own personality, activated by wearing; it overshadows the wearer's personality and may bring trance in which its spirit takes over; the mask wears your body and is responsible for what happens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 152-153; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMaskPossession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Overshadowing and possession by a mask spirit"@en, "Überschattung und Besessenheit durch einen Maskengeist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mask-work can bring overshadowing as well as complete possession."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 152; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMaskSpeechLessons a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Masks develop like persons (after Johnstone)"@en, "Masken entwickeln sich wie Personen (nach Johnstone)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Per mask teacher Keith Johnstone, new masks lack bodily skills and speech and need speech lessons; they acquire gestures, props and postures; they may be playful, aggressive or lewd, unlike for the user."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMeetingYourOwnDemons a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Meeting your own demons through masks"@en, "Begegnung mit den eigenen Dämonen durch Masken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Out-of-character mask behaviour can powerfully confront you with your own demons and show that not all your possible behaviour fits your self-image."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRitualMasks a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Masks in ritual: leaders, groups, guardians"@en, "Masken im Ritual: Anführer, Gruppen, Wächter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Masks can lead rituals as invoked spirit or sabbat leader; groups of masks develop myths and perform for an unmasked audience; masks on stands facing inward serve as participating guardians of a ritual site, which commonly call out wanting to join in."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFullFaceHalfFaceMasks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Full-face versus half-face masks"@en, "Vollmasken gegenüber Halbmasken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Full-face masks have no mouth and communicate physically; half-face masks, once they learn to speak, hardly stop."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 153; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMaskWorkNotCold a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Mask-work needs a leader; never cold"@en, "Maskenarbeit braucht einen Leiter; nie kalt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mask-work is not to be done cold: a leader should always direct it, anchoring anyone who fears it is becoming too much and letting participants feel safe enough to let the mask take over; preludes such as Animals and Faces precede it."@en ;
    skos:note "The text sets the rule without a stated consequence of skipping it, and the strength is entered as a prescribed order."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAnimalsGame, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFacesExercise ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMaskPossession ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 154; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAnimalsGame a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Animals game"@en, "Tierspiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group members take animal roles and act them with noises and gestures; mostly stereotyped, but some get caught up, so it can prelude shape-shifting work."@en ;
    skos:note "Prelude to mask-work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 154; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFacesExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Faces exercise"@en, "Gesichter-Übung"@de ;
    skos:definition "All make a wordless emotional noise, then make and hold the matching face, mill about for some minutes, stop and share feedback."@en ;
    skos:note "Prelude to mask-work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 154-155; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFacialChangeSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Marked facial change during invocation"@en, "Deutliche Gesichtsveränderung während der Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "A person invoking or being invoked into often shows marked facial changes, a positive indicator of momentarily becoming someone other than the everyday persona."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: marked changes in the face of the person invoking, or of the person into whom an entity is invoked, which others can observe. No deadline. It concerns invocation generally, as in pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAssumptionOfGodForms."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 155; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFacePainting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Face- and body-painting"@en, "Gesichts- und Körperbemalung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Paint the face, even subtly, to prepare for masks and enhance invocation, as an ancient way to invoke and project an image; extend to body-painting, e.g. for the animals exercise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 155; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCPropsExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Props exercise"@en, "Requisiten-Übung"@de ;
    skos:definition "One person gives each group member a single prop to use to suggest a character or stereotype (poncho, mirror-shades, shabby coat), shown through posture, movement, voice and manner."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 155; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPropsYieldFlexibility a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Prop work yields flexibility in taking on personalities"@en, "Requisitenarbeit bewirkt Beweglichkeit im Annehmen von Persönlichkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Making oneself into other characters with a single prop is said to help overcome habitual patterns and to make one more flexible in assuming personalities in group and solo work."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCPropsExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRoleFlexibility ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 155; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRoleFlexibility a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Flexibility in assuming personalities"@en, "Flexibilität im Annehmen von Persönlichkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ease of making oneself into other characters, overcoming habitual patterns and being more flexible in group and solo work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 155; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCLettingTheMaskWorkYieldsPossession a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Not thinking lets the mask take over"@en, "Nicht-Denken lässt die Maske übernehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When thinking is stopped, for instance by humming while donning the mask, the mask's own personality may rise from the Deep Mind and do the work."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCLettingTheMaskWork ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMaskPossession ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCLettingTheMaskWork a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the mask act (humming)"@en, "Die Maske arbeiten lassen (Summen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of thinking yourself into the mask's role, cease thinking and allow the mask to act, letting its personality rise from the Deep Mind while waking awareness is distracted, e.g. by humming loudly while putting it on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMaskWorkPrecautions a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Approach mask-work carefully; banish to close"@en, "Maskenarbeit vorsichtig angehen; mit Bannung schließen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mask-work must be approached carefully if at all and respected as powerful; a banishing ritual is a useful way to close group sessions."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRitualMasks ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSoloMaskWork a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Solo mask-work as aid to invocation"@en, "Maskenarbeit allein als Hilfe zur Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use a mask in solo meditation or ritual, especially for invoking an entity; a full-face mask alters movement and attention; ritual donning heightens the sense of the sacred and the mask comes to recall the ritual's feelings and symbols."@en ;
    skos:note "Mask-trance usually less intense than in groups."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 156; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCChainsOfAssociation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation works through chains of association"@en, "Invokation wirkt durch Assoziationsketten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like other magic, invocation builds chains of association, so incense, oils, food, drink, colours and clothing are worth considering; smell evokes memories and arousal immediately."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 156-157; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCIncenseOffering a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Incense and scent for ritual atmosphere"@en, "Weihrauch und Duft für rituelle Atmosphäre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use incense and perfume offerings to build atmosphere and invoke deities, choosing scents to evoke the desired ambiance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 157; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCScentApproaches a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three approaches to choosing scents for a deity"@en, "Drei Wege, Düfte für eine Gottheit zu wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Historical authenticity; magical correspondences fixed by an authority; or the Tao of choosing whatever you judge fitting, including artificial evocative smells such as a dentist's waiting room."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 157; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSacramentalFoodAndDrink a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sacramental food and drink"@en, "Sakramentale Speisen und Getränke"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use food and drink as sacraments to absorb the essence of the invoked entity, fitted to the ritual (mead in Northern tradition, rum for some Loa); in Dionysian rite drinking itself invokes; consume offerings as grounding and close with feasting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, pp. 157-158; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRobedOrSkyclad a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Robe or skyclad"@en, "Robe oder himmelsbekleidet"@de ;
    skos:definition "A hooded robe conceals the body outline and marks the act as different; working naked raises body-image issues for newcomers but makes the skin a better sense organ and the worker more alert."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 158; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDressingThePart a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dressing the part"@en, "Sich passend kleiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rather than only visualising divine garb, use costumes, masks and face paint for invocatory ritual; preparing them may reward as much as the rite."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 158; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCLiveSound a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Live sound beats recorded music"@en, "Live-Klang schlägt aufgezeichnete Musik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recorded music adds ambiance, but producing the sounds yourself is unbeatable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 159; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCIynx a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Iynx (whirler)"@en, "Iynx (Schwirrrad)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A small wheel on a string loop; wind and let it unwind to spin humming; historically employed to invoke or banish deities, draw them into a celebrant, draw down the Moon, rain-making, binding demons, love magic."@en ;
    skos:note "Historical uses reported, not prescribed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 159; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBullroarer a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Bullroarer"@en, "Schwirrholz"@de ;
    skos:definition "A chamfered piece of heavy wood at least ten inches long on a thick cord, whirled overhead for a drone or rushing hum; outdoors only."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 159; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBullroarerCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Bullroarer can hit onlookers"@en, "Schwirrholz kann Zuschauer treffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stand where unwary onlookers cannot be struck."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBullroarer ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 159; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRhythmMakers a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Rhythm-makers: drums, shakers, handclaps, bells"@en, "Rhythmusgeber: Trommeln, Rasseln, Klatschen, Glocken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Create rhythms with drums, shakers or claps, the simplest and often most effective enhancement of invocation; handclaps, bells or gongs punctuate ritual stages in post-Golden Dawn style."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 159; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDrummingPossession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession by a spirit via drumming"@en, "Besessenheit durch einen Geist mittels Trommeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drumming can carry a celebrant into spirit possession."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 159; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDrummingYieldsPossession a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Drumming can bring on possession"@en, "Trommeln kann Besessenheit herbeiführen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drumming alone is said to be able to carry a celebrant into being possessed by a spirit."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRhythmMakers ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDrummingPossession ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 159; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSustainedNotes a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sustained notes: singing bowl, gong, breath instruments"@en, "Gehaltene Töne: Klangschale, Gong, Blasinstrumente"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rub a Tibetan singing bell rim fast with a wooden block for a sustained tone, tap a gong softly, or use didgeridoo, bugle, whistle, conch or thighbone trumpet."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 8 Kali in the Disco, p. 159; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .


#
# Chapter 9, Conquering Demons
#

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPersonalDemons a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal demons as unintegrated complexes (Kleshas)"@en, "Persönliche Dämonen als unintegrierte Komplexe (Kleshas)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Latent psychic structures, unresolved complexes and suppressed voices raised defensively by the ego, acting seemingly independently; habitual emotional or behavioural patterns, problematic because not integrated; in Tantra called Kleshas. They are blocks of behaviour summoned by stressful situations, e.g. the Jealousy Demon."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 160; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCJealousyDemonNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Jealousy Demon"@en, "Eifersuchtsdämon"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not a tentacled monster from elsewhere but a response pattern that erupts in accusations when evidence seems to confirm one's fears."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Jealousy Demon" ;
    pm:nameRole "personal demon (intrapsychic complex)" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 160; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDemonBinding a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal demons can be identified, bound and transformed"@en, "Persönliche Dämonen können erkannt, gebunden und verwandelt werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unlike grimoire demons they often lack shape, sigil or name, yet like them they can be recognised, bound and magically transformed to work for us."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 160; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDemonAsExcuse a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Using a demon as excuse for behaviour"@en, "Den Dämon als Ausrede benutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If you use your demon to excuse behaviour you will not take responsibility for, you have gone seriously astray; it admits the demon controls you more than you control it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNamingPersonalDemon ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDemonAsExcuseFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Excusing tantrums by the demon shows it controls you"@en, "Rechtfertigung mit dem Dämon zeigt dessen Kontrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blaming one's demon for a tantrum is a sign the demon has more control than you."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: excusing one's behaviour by one's demon shows that the demon holds more control than the magician. No deadline; the failure is put on the operator. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNamingPersonalDemon."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNamingPersonalDemon a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Isolating and naming a personal demon"@en, "Einen persönlichen Dämon isolieren und benennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Isolate the knot of inner talk, attitudes, fears, reflexes and fantasies; give it its own name, shape and sigil; then observe the circumstances in which it appears, including how your feelings, others' responses and your perception of them feed it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEverydayDemons a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyday occurrence makes personal demons harder to handle"@en, "Alltägliches Auftreten erschwert den Umgang mit persönlichen Dämonen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because personal demons appear in daily life rather than in the sealed setting of ritual, they are often harder to deal with."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSummoningPersonalDemon a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Recalling a demon-provoking situation"@en, "Vergegenwärtigen einer dämonenauslösenden Situation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make yourself comfortable and bring to mind a situation that summons a demon you find hard to subdue, any response you would like to handle differently."@en ;
    skos:note "Introduced with Crowley's remark that demons are easy to summon."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBodilyGnosisLoop a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Demons ride a feedback loop of bodily arousal and context"@en, "Dämonen reiten eine Rückkopplung aus Körpererregung und Kontext"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stress triggers demons; fight/flight, fear, anger and depression arise from physical stimulation, a bodily gnosis, in a feedback loop with the context; demons are tied to knots of bodily tension that tighten with each appearance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCShortCircuitFirst a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "First short-circuit the loop of anxiety and response"@en, "Zuerst den Kreislauf aus Angst und Reaktion kurzschließen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first stage in turning a demon from an overwhelming experience into something understood and bound to the will is to break the feedback loop between bodily anxiety and the responses of mind and emotion; Emotional Engineering is the method given for it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCEmotionalEngineering ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDemonBinding ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 161; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCEmotionalEngineering a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Emotional Engineering"@en, "Emotionale Technik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualise a worst-case demon situation while noticing bodily arousal; then, whenever gripped by strong emotion: (1) do not suppress it, experience it fully; (2) note physical sensations as it rises; (3) still the inner dialogue's fantasies and memories that feed it; (4) attend to bodily sensation alone, refusing to label it as any emotion, treating it as an undefined odd sensation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 161-162; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFreeEmotion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Free Emotion"@en, "Freie Emotion"@de ;
    skos:definition "A state of unlabelled arousal which can be redefined, e.g. as pleasure or ecstasy; useful in Ego Magic generally and especially for starving personal demons of power."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 162; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEmotionalEngineeringYieldsFreeEmotion a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Emotional Engineering yields Free Emotion"@en, "Emotionale Technik bewirkt Freie Emotion"@de ;
    skos:definition "The four-step process leads towards Free Emotion and deprives demons of power."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCEmotionalEngineering ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFreeEmotion ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 162; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCollusiveDemons a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Demons are layered and collude with each other"@en, "Dämonen sind geschichtet und verbünden sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Demons are behavioural and cognitive as well as physiological (e.g. smoking excuses and rationalisations); they are contextual and collude to survive, as when a struggling drinker offers drink to another, or a Jealousy demon and a partner's Fear-of-Restriction demon feed each other."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 162-163; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGaneshaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Ganesha"@en, "Ganesha"@de ;
    skos:definition "Popular Indian deity prayed to before all worship; invoked to remove obstacles, bring luck, prosperity in commerce, liberation; vermilion, elephant-headed, four hands with tusk, noose, goad and boon-giving gesture, pomegranate in trunk, crescent moon, serpent round split belly, mouse vehicle; binder of demons, playful dancing Puckish son of Shiva and Parvati, freedom personified, wise without ponderousness. Symbolism: belly as universe, winnowing ears sifting truth, trunk as discrimination and OM, broken tusk as divine sacrifice, mouse as small desires and doubts (kleshas) and cunning."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Ganesha", "Ganapati" ;
    pm:nameRole "deity binding and transforming obsessional demons" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 163-165; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAbhimaansuraNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Abhimaansura"@en, "Abhimaansura"@de ;
    skos:definition "The demon of egotistic pride, one of the obsessional demons that incarnations of Ganesha are said to have fought and subdued, as Hine reports from a Purana he names Upa Parana."@en ;
    skos:note "The text announces eight incarnations of Ganesha but names seven demons; \"Upa Parana\" is printed so."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Abhimaansura" ;
    pm:nameRole "obsessional demon of egotistic pride, overcome by an incarnation of Ganesha" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 164; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCKaamaasuraNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Kaamaasura"@en, "Kaamaasura"@de ;
    skos:definition "The demon of lust, one of the obsessional demons that incarnations of Ganesha are said to have fought and subdued, as Hine reports from a Purana he names Upa Parana."@en ;
    skos:note "The text announces eight incarnations of Ganesha but names seven demons; \"Upa Parana\" is printed so."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Kaamaasura" ;
    pm:nameRole "obsessional demon of lust, overcome by an incarnation of Ganesha" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 164; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCKrodhaasuraNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Krodhaasura"@en, "Krodhaasura"@de ;
    skos:definition "The demon of unjust anger, one of the obsessional demons that incarnations of Ganesha are said to have fought and subdued, as Hine reports from a Purana he names Upa Parana."@en ;
    skos:note "The text announces eight incarnations of Ganesha but names seven demons; \"Upa Parana\" is printed so."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Krodhaasura" ;
    pm:nameRole "obsessional demon of unjust anger, overcome by an incarnation of Ganesha" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 164; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCLobhaasuraNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Lobhaasura"@en, "Lobhaasura"@de ;
    skos:definition "The demon of greed, one of the obsessional demons that incarnations of Ganesha are said to have fought and subdued, as Hine reports from a Purana he names Upa Parana."@en ;
    skos:note "The text announces eight incarnations of Ganesha but names seven demons; \"Upa Parana\" is printed so."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Lobhaasura" ;
    pm:nameRole "obsessional demon of greed, overcome by an incarnation of Ganesha" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 164; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMaatsaraNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Maatsara"@en, "Maatsara"@de ;
    skos:definition "The demon of jealousy, one of the obsessional demons that incarnations of Ganesha are said to have fought and subdued, as Hine reports from a Purana he names Upa Parana."@en ;
    skos:note "The text announces eight incarnations of Ganesha but names seven demons; \"Upa Parana\" is printed so."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Maatsara" ;
    pm:nameRole "obsessional demon of jealousy, overcome by an incarnation of Ganesha" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
