pmp:ChaosMagicCondCGaneshaBellyMeditation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meditating on Ganesha dancing in the belly"@en, "Meditation über den in Bauch tanzenden Ganesha"@de ;
    skos:definition "Set Ganesha within your belly and contemplate his ecstatic dancing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 164; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCLakshmiGanapatiNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Lakshmi Ganapati with Siddhi and Buddhi"@en, "Lakshmi Ganapati mit Siddhi und Buddhi"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ganesha as giver of success, flanked by Siddhi (achievement) and Buddhi (wisdom); Tantric icons may show him with a Shakti."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Lakshmi Ganapati", "Siddhi", "Buddhi" ;
    pm:nameRole "aspect of Ganesha as success-giver and his consorts" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 164; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDiscrimination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Discrimination is the first great lesson; liberation by attention"@en, "Unterscheidung als erste große Lektion; Befreiung durch Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ganesha's trunk stands for discrimination, called the first major lesson of any aspiring magician; a Tantric reading of his ears holds that liberation comes from attending to what is around you, stilling inner chatter and meeting the world as it actually is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 164-165; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCGaneshaDemonMorphing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ganesha Demon-Morphing"@en, "Ganesha-Dämonenverwandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Relax, attend to body, turn inward to the belly as a void of red mist; with the breath let Ganesha form there while repeating Om Ganapati Namah; then become Ganesha yourself (trunk, ears, outline); visualise a demon-stirring situation inside your belly with yourself in it; feel the body as pure unlabelled sensation, breathing slow and deep; turn the sensation into growing pleasure and power until it must be voiced; repeat the sound and keep any word or mantra that forms; finish with the Elephant Dance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 165-166; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCElephantDance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elephant Dance"@en, "Elefantentanz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Let the head loll from side to side with loose neck and swing the torso left and right, like elephants at a watering hole, to keep residual tension from settling after the catharsis."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 166; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDemonMorphingYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Demon-Morphing yields release and recognition"@en, "Dämonenverwandlung bewirkt Lösung und Erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercise is said to be useful in two ways: freeing from lingering responses and learning to recognise a demon's loop."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCGaneshaDemonMorphing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCReleaseFromDemonicResponse, pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDemonFeedbackPoints ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 166; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCReleaseFromDemonicResponse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Release from a lingering demonic response"@en, "Lösung aus einer anhaltenden dämonischen Reaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Freeing oneself from a demonic reaction that persists after the trigger has passed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 166; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDemonFeedbackPoints a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognising a demon's feedback points"@en, "Erkennen der Rückkopplungspunkte eines Dämons"@de ;
    skos:definition "Learning the characteristic thoughts, feelings and behaviour of a demon, noticing when it carries you away, and so breaking its loops more easily."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 166; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPlayfulRelaxation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Playful relaxation beats grim determination in Ego Magic"@en, "Spielerische Entspannung schlägt grimmige Entschlossenheit in der Ich-Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most Ego magic seems most effective approached from playful relaxation, which is why the playful Ganesha suits it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 166; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCStopLookRelaxWord a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Stop-Look-Relax word"@en, "Stopp-Schau-Entspann-Wort"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualise a demon situation and let it carry you off; then see Ganesha tower above, trumpeting so the blast rips apart thoughts and images and vibrates through you until it becomes a sound you can make; voice it until clear. Thereafter hurl this sound at a rising demon to stop it and stop yourself feeding it, then relax and view the situation calmly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 166-167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCStopWordYieldsHalt a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The Stop-Look-Relax word halts a rising demon"@en, "Das Stopp-Schau-Entspann-Wort hält einen aufsteigenden Dämon an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hurling the sound at a demon as it rises is meant to halt it at once and to keep the operator from feeding it through fantasy and other reactions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCStopLookRelaxWord ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCHaltingDemon ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCHaltingDemon a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Halting a rising demon"@en, "Anhalten eines aufsteigenden Dämons"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stopping a demon in its tracks and ceasing to feed it through fantasy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRelaxingInPresenceSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxing in the demon's presence: halfway to making it work for you"@en, "Entspannt in Gegenwart des Dämons: halb am Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ceasing to feed a demon and relaxing while it is present puts you halfway to making it serve you, like Ganesha riding the mouse."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: being able to stop feeding a demon and to relax in its presence, called halfway to making it serve you. No deadline; felt from within. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCStopLookRelaxWord."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDemonDialogue a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dialogue with a demon, layer by layer"@en, "Dialog mit dem Dämon, Schicht um Schicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once calm after hurling the word, enter into dialogue with the demon, which defends itself against being found out and dissolved; like a Russian doll it can be stripped in layers, showing what part it plays in keeping you as you are, and it may then be worked with in a new way."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMagicalResponses a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical Responses to personal demons"@en, "Magische Antworten auf persönliche Dämonen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's four responses: Feed to Exhaustion, Offer It Death, Demonic Pacts, Banishing with Extreme Prejudice."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 167-170; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFeedToExhaustion a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Feed to Exhaustion"@en, "Bis zur Erschöpfung füttern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of suppressing the demon, let it rage through you in every manifestation, pursuing its fantasies (e.g. revenge plans) to absurd lengths until exhausted, since demons keep power by stopping us from following through all the outcomes of the fears they raise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFeedToExhaustionJealousy a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Hine's jealousy fed to exhaustion"@en, "Hines bis zur Erschöpfung gefütterte Eifersucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine let a jealousy possession rage through him, generating absurd revenge plans, until exhausted, after which the trigger seemed unimportant and laughable."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFeedToExhaustion ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCTriggerLosesImportance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCTriggerLosesImportance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trigger loses importance"@en, "Auslöser verliert an Bedeutung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The trigger of the possession no longer matters, even seems laughable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCOfferItDeath a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Offer It Death"@en, "Ihm den Tod anbieten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Surprise a demon into immobility by offering it death, as by threatening to kill yourself and reaching for a razor or sword; the presence of real death puts everything else in context, and since demons shun dying they are likely to freeze, if the offer is meant, so that they can be examined closely."@en ;
    skos:note "The text attaches no safety caution to this technique, and none is entered."@en ;
    skos:note "The condition that the offer be meant is part of this practice; it was recorded at first as a separate prerequisite and is folded in here, since no prior step stands apart from the practice itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCOfferItDeathYieldsFreezing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Offering death freezes a demon"@en, "Das Todesangebot lässt einen Dämon erstarren"@de ;
    skos:definition "A demon offered death in earnest is said to be likely to freeze, so that it can be examined closely."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCOfferItDeath ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFrozenDemon ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFrozenDemon a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freezing a demon for examination"@en, "Einfrieren eines Dämons zur Untersuchung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The demon becomes immobile so it can be examined closely."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 167; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDemonicPactsFolklore a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against occult folklore forbidding pacts with demons"@en, "Gegen okkulte Überlieferung, die Pakte mit Dämonen verbietet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Common occult folklore warns that pacts with demons are dangerous because the demonic belongs to the lower self and should be banished; Hine likens this to Victorian ankle-covering and argues repression empowers demons, which are too useful an energy source to banish or to give free rein."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the folklore he argues against is not cited from any work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 168; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRepressedDemonCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Repressed demons grow stronger"@en, "Unterdrückte Dämonen werden stärker"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repressing a demon makes it stronger and uncontrollable."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDemonBinding ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 168; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDemonicPact a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Demonic Pact"@en, "Dämonenpakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Expose the demon: identify its sensations, thoughts, behaviour and muscular tension, treat it as a shape and personality with magical name and sigil; deliberately relive a situation where it overwhelmed you to see the reciprocal relationship; then in the simplest pact acknowledge it and turn its action into something that strengthens the free play of your power, e.g. anger into creativity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 168-169; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCExposureBeforePact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Expose the demon before a pact"@en, "Den Dämon vor dem Pakt bloßlegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A pact requires that the demon first be exposed and identified; such realisations are rarely pleasant because they involve owning responsibility for it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNamingPersonalDemon ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDemonicPact ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 168; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCurseIntoInvention a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Curse impulse turned into magical invention"@en, "Fluchimpuls in magische Erfindung verwandelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tempted to curse someone, Hine seeks an ingenious unique curse; the wish for revenge is replaced by the wish to create something new (e.g. the viral servitors of Chapter Six) and the anger is forgotten."@en ;
    skos:note "The viral servitors are described in chapter 6 of the book, outside this section."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDemonicPact ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRedirectedDemonPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 168-169; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCNegativeEmotionNotDemonic a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not label all negative emotions demonic"@en, "Nicht alle negativen Gefühle als dämonisch etikettieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is a tempting mistake to label negative responses as demons; anger may be legitimate, and what matters is how it is expressed, e.g. a pattern of suppression then outburst is the dysfunction to work on."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNamingPersonalDemon ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 169; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRedirectedDemonPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Redirecting a demon's power (anger into creativity)"@en, "Umleitung der Dämonenkraft (Zorn in Kreativität)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A demon's energy channelled to enhance one's own power; satisfying because both work together."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 169; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCalmAngerOffice a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Calm statement of anger stops escalation (office anecdote)"@en, "Ruhige Äußerung des Zorns beendet Eskalation (Büroanekdote)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of suppressing annoyance until shouting, Hine once stated his anger calmly and plainly to a colleague; she stopped, and he conveyed his feelings without tension or carrying anger afterwards."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCDemonicPact ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRedirectedDemonPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 169; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCOthersDemonsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Emotional attachment prevents effective exorcism of others' demons"@en, "Emotionale Bindung verhindert wirksamen Exorzismus fremder Dämonen"@de ;
    skos:definition "How far one can integrate others' demons is doubtful; addiction demons have more influence on their hosts than you will, prove their panacea more reliable, and will try to pull you into the host's patterns; attachment rules out the needed detachment, objectivity and cruelty."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBanishingWithExtremePrejudice ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 169-170; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBanishingWithExtremePrejudice a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing with Extreme Prejudice"@en, "Bannen mit äußerster Entschiedenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "When a friend or lover is in the grip of a dysfunctional demon (jealousy, possessiveness, alcohol, heroin, violence), do not try to be their exorcist: banish the demon, get it out and keep it out, separating addict and demon in your mind, if only to show the demon you are aware of it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 169-170; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPersonalGenius a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal Genius under many names"@en, "Persönlicher Genius unter vielen Namen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The creative wellspring of power and inspiration is variously called God or an Archangel by healers, the Knowledge and Conversation of one's Holy Guardian Angel by magicians, Higher Self by therapists; Hine finds Crowley's Moonchild the most useful reference."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 170; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFeedingTheFire a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeding the Fire"@en, "Das Feuer nähren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine your body hollow with a flickering flame inside that feeds on all experience: each breath, moment of awareness, emotion, thought, victory, defeat, identification and revulsion becomes its fuel."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 170; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFeedingTheFireYieldsNonAttachment a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Feeding the Fire aims at non-attachment"@en, "Das Feuer nähren zielt auf Nichtanhaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "The aim of this and similar exercises is said to be some measure of non-attachment to one's actions and works."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFeedingTheFire ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCNonAttachment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 170; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCNonAttachment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-attachment to one's actions"@en, "Nichtanhaften an den eigenen Taten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Such exercises aim at some measure of detachment from one's actions and works; the flame is Kundalini-Shakti, the organising creative power present in humans and stars, from which the power to illuminate comes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 170; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCHollowPipe a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Claiming the power as one's own weakens it"@en, "Die Kraft als eigene zu beanspruchen schwächt sie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The power is not under ego control; tendencies to identify it as exclusively yours weaken its expression; cultivate the attitude of being a hollow pipe through which it flows freely by removing identifications and blocks."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFeedingTheFire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 170; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCChannelersCritique a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against New Age channelers"@en, "Gegen New-Age-Channeler"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine ridicules channeled spirit guides, masters and space beings whose message is always love and harmony in pseudo-scientific jargon (Ramtha named), whose address changes with fashion (Spiritualist Indian guides, Theosophical Tibetan Masters, saucer gods, dolphins), and holds that channelers lack discrimination and channel the higher-authority programs of their own culture; New Age consciousness is called one more Slave-God swindle, an escape that never challenges the ego."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read; the channelled teachings he mocks are not cited from any work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 171-172, 175; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCChanneledEntitiesCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Contact with wisdom-entities useful only up to a point"@en, "Kontakt mit Weisheitswesen nur bis zu einem Punkt nützlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Contact with channeled entities can help, but only so far; discrimination is very necessary in any human-entity communication; messages are not automatically benign."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCWindowsIntoChaos ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 171-172; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRamthaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Ramtha"@en, "Ramtha"@de ;
    skos:definition "Channeled entity cited as a source of platitudes promising to heal mental troubles."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Ramtha" ;
    pm:nameRole "New Age channeled entity (derided)" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 171; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDiscriminationBeforeContact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Discrimination before approaching communications from higher entities"@en, "Unterscheidung vor dem Umgang mit Mitteilungen höherer Wesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Discrimination, which channelers are said to lack, is called very necessary whenever one approaches what passes between humans and higher entities; magicians of post-Golden Dawn systems are said to bring healthy scepticism to inner-plane contacts and to test them."@en ;
    skos:note "The text calls the quality necessary but names no consequence of lacking it beyond the contrast with the channelers, and the strength is entered as a prescribed order."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDiscrimination ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCContactVerification ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 172; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCThelemicContactTest a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Testing a contact with the Law of Thelema"@en, "Prüfen eines Kontakts mit dem Gesetz von Thelema"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thelemic magicians test a contact by pronouncing the formula of the Law of Thelema; a genuine contact answers with the fitting rejoinder."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 172; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFalseContactFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "False contact fails the test"@en, "Falscher Kontakt besteht die Prüfung nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "A false entity fails to give the rejoinder and flees screaming into an astral gap."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: an entity that gives no fitting reply to the Thelemic formula, or flees, counts as a false contact. No deadline; the failure is put on the target, the entity, and not on the operator or the test. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCThelemicContactTest."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 172; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAASealTest a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Projecting the A.A. seal onto an entity"@en, "Projizieren des A.A.-Siegels auf eine Wesenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "As a check, project the A.A. seal onto the entity mentally."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 172; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCGematriaCrossExamination a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cross-examining entities by symbolism and gematria"@en, "Kreuzverhör von Wesenheiten mittels Symbolik und Gematria"@de ;
    skos:definition "Question the entity using symbolism and gematria; with ritual techniques this helps ensure invoked beings are who they claim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 172; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCContactTestsYieldVerification a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Contact tests help verify an entity's identity"@en, "Kontaktprüfungen helfen, die Identität eines Wesens zu sichern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Thelemic formula, the projected seal and cross-examination by symbolism and gematria, together with ritual techniques, are said to help ensure that invoked beings are who they claim to be."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCThelemicContactTest, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAASealTest, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCGematriaCrossExamination ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCContactVerification ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 172; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCContactVerification a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Verifying the identity of invoked beings"@en, "Identitätsprüfung angerufener Wesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ensuring that invoked beings are who they claim to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 172; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMeaningfulCommunicationSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Communications that make sense and inform"@en, "Mitteilungen, die Sinn ergeben und informieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine demands that communications make sense at least in terms of his recent work; valuable messages are informative, giving pointers on an issue or internally consistent symbolic messages, rather than cosmic platitudes; such messages concern only the recipient."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: communications that make sense in terms of what the recipient has lately been doing and give pointers on an issue or internally consistent symbolism, rather than platitudes. Hine's own criterion; no deadline."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 172-173; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCommunicationDegeneration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Degeneration of channeled communications with ego-involvement"@en, "Verfall gechannelter Mitteilungen mit Ich-Beteiligung"@de ;
    skos:definition "First contacts may give startling syntheses, but the more the recipient identifies with the entity, the more the messages decay into obvious cosmic mush, followed by self-proclamation as priest of exclusive mysteries and founding a world-saving cult."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: messages decline into obvious cosmic platitudes as the recipient's ego-involvement with the entity grows, ending in a self-proclaimed priesthood and a small cult. No deadline, a decline over time; the failure is put on the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 173; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEntitiesNeitherObjectiveNorFictitious a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Entities neither wholly objective nor fictitious"@en, "Wesenheiten weder ganz objektiv noch fiktiv"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against channeler literalism and sceptic dismissal, a magician holds entities are not wholly objective yet not fictitious; imagination is not less real. Model from Gibson's Neuromancer: an AI builds personality constructs from humans' memories as masks to interface with them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 173-174; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCosmicDoctrineReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "Dion Fortune's Cosmic Doctrine communicators"@en, "Die Mitteiler von Dion Fortunes Cosmic Doctrine"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine quotes the Cosmic Doctrine, where inner-plane beings say humans cannot grasp what they are but may imagine them on the astral plane, through which contact happens, the picture unreal but its results real."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Dion Fortune" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "inner-plane communicators addressing Dion Fortune" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Not described in the quotation; Hine adds only that Fortune drew heavily on inner-plane contacts in working out her magical ideas." ;
    skos:note "Hine ascribes this to a work he names and does not cite by edition: Dion Fortune, The Cosmic Doctrine, quoted in Hine, Condensed Chaos (New Falcon, 1995), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 174; no edition or page of the original is given. The node holds what Condensed Chaos reports; the named work is reachable in its own right and is not read here, so the node is entered as Hine's ascription and not as a mediated reading of that work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 174; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDavidCarsonsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "David Carsons"@en, "David Carsons"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner-plane contact of Dion Fortune, claimed as a young British officer killed in WWI; Alan Richardson's research (Priestess) found he never existed; Hine reads him as a construct generated from Fortune's magic, an interface for information."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "David Carsons" ;
    pm:nameRole "inner-plane contact; construct" ;
    skos:note "Hine ascribes this to a work he names and does not cite by edition: Alan Richardson, Priestess (his biography of Dion Fortune), as reported in Hine, Condensed Chaos (New Falcon, 1995), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 174; no edition or page is given. The node holds what Condensed Chaos reports; the named work is reachable in its own right and is not read here, so the node is entered as Hine's ascription and not as a mediated reading of that work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 174; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCWindowsIntoChaos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner-plane entities as windows into chaos"@en, "Innere-Ebenen-Wesen als Fenster ins Chaos"@de ;
    skos:definition "Extending one's sphere of knowledge needs windows translating raw data into meaning; entities are how we conceive these windows, appearing independent to make sense of the data, with personalities matching the recipient's beliefs; they are emergent properties of information-processing meeting what lies beyond, not pathological secondary personalities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 174-175; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCEntityOutposts a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Generating entities by will as outposts"@en, "Erzeugung von Wesenheiten durch Willen als Außenposten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Usually entities arise automatically as will and imagination focus on a vector, but they can be generated deliberately as outposts in which one's own ideas and inner worlds may be explored and integrated into one's psychocosm."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, pp. 174-175; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInnerworldContactsEdge a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magicians' contacts serve going beyond limits"@en, "Kontakte von Magiern dienen dem Überschreiten von Grenzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Magicians use innerworld contacts to push repeatedly over their edges and sift insights from abysses, a difference of degree from channelers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 9 Conquering Demons, p. 175; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .


#
# Chapter 10, Are You Illuminated?
#

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMagicAsChange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic as a means of change needing context"@en, "Magie als Mittel des Wandels, das Kontext braucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "However described, magic brings about change; for change to be effective you must set the effects of your work in context and integrate them, which needs a sense of past and direction; initiation names this integration, and Illumination is among its chief by-products."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 176; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiationAsProcess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiation as a recurring threshold of change"@en, "Initiation als wiederkehrende Schwelle des Wandels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Initiation is a threshold of change met many times in life, with peaks (initiatory crises), troughs (dark night) and plateaus; its key is recognising you have reached a turning point and are in transition; knowing one's own change cycles and how to ride them out is central to magical practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 176-177; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCThresholdRecognition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognising that one stands at a threshold of change"@en, "Erkennen, dass man an einer Schwelle des Wandels steht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being aware that one has reached a turning point, a crossroads between past and future, and is in a period of transition; the chapter calls this recognition the key to initiation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 177, 181, 183; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCTransitionPatternShedding a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Consciously shedding and adopting patterns at transitions"@en, "Bewusstes Ablegen und Annehmen von Mustern an Übergängen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conscious awareness of entering a transition may let one discard outdated behavioural and emotional patterns and take up new ones."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 177; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiatoryStages a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stages of the initiatory process (after Campbell)"@en, "Stadien des Initiationsprozesses (nach Campbell)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The stages of initiation as the chapter takes them in turn: crisis and call, the journey into the wilderness, the initiatory sickness, the dark night, macro- and micro-initiations, fear and relaxing into it, spontaneity, the innerworld confrontations of the descent, and death-rebirth with illumination; Hine says such stages have been charted by students of myth, Joseph Campbell among them, chiefly for shamanic initiation, and holds them to apply to other areas of life."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos, drawing on the mapping he credits to anthropologists such as Joseph Campbell" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 177-190; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCrisisAndCall a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Crisis and call"@en, "Krise und Ruf"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first stage is a personal crisis and call: vision, dreams, or a disturbing urge to see beyond normal life, often after intense religious, spiritual or political experience, or existential unease; it takes one over the wall of the social world and disrupts work, relationships and values."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 177-178; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRefusingTheCall a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Refusing the call can bring further crises"@en, "Verweigerung des Rufes kann weitere Krisen bringen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In tribal societies refusing the call to shamanic training is no small thing and can bring more crises, even death."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCrisisAndCall ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 178; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSpiritualPathAddiction a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Spiritual urgency and addiction to paths"@en, "Spirituelle Dringlichkeit und Pfadsucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those feeling the summons often feel urgent need to become enlightened or change the world, can become addicted to spiritual paths and as tiresome as any messianic convert, may misread friends' reactions, and are prey to cults that brand critics false friends."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCrisisAndCall ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 178; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiatoryIsolation a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Isolation, alienation and nostalgia at the start of the journey"@en, "Isolation, Entfremdung und Nostalgie zu Beginn der Reise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving out to the margin of one's culture brings isolation and alienation, regret and nostalgia for the lost clear-cut former life."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCCrisisAndCall ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 178; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCJourneyIntoTheWilderness a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Journey into the wilderness / deliberate isolation"@en, "Reise in die Wildnis / bewusste Isolation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Withdraw from fellows and consensus reality, physically as the proto-shaman does, or for Westerners on the plane of ideas, questioning everything and perhaps withdrawing from social relations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 178-179; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCWildernessYieldsLoosening a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Deliberate isolation loosens fixed beliefs"@en, "Bewusste Isolation lockert feste Überzeugungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Withdrawing from one's fellows is called a strong means of loosening the sense of holding fixed values and beliefs."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCJourneyIntoTheWilderness ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCLooseningFixedBeliefs ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCLooseningFixedBeliefs a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Loosening fixed values and beliefs"@en, "Lockerung fester Werte und Überzeugungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deliberate isolation is said to be a powerful way of loosening one's sense of fixed values and beliefs; social deprivation appears in many magical cultures."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiatorySickness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiatory sickness as difficult but useful development"@en, "Initiationskrankheit als schwierige, aber nützliche Entwicklung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The summons is often heralded by sudden or creeping initiatory sickness with fits and strange behaviour; tribal cultures see it as useful development, and research is said to show shamans become the healthiest people in their tribes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiatorySicknessLabelling a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against psychiatric labelling of shamans and its anti-psychiatry reversal"@en, "Gegen psychiatrische Etikettierung von Schamanen und deren antipsychiatrische Umkehrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine rejects past anthropological and psychological labelling of shamans as psychotic, schizophrenic or epileptic as ethnocentric, notes the reverse error of enthusiasts calling such patients proto-shamans, and blames the western notion that anything beyond ordinary consciousness is pathological."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 179; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDarkNightOfTheSoul a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dark Night of the Soul"@en, "Dunkle Nacht der Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quoting the mystic St John of the Cross, Hine describes a state of spiritual dryness and depression which binds imagination and empties the faculties; Hine holds it brings the soul to stillness for deep transformation, reflected by the Tarot Moon card, and rejects the view that such experiences should be avoided."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 180; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCTheHump a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The hump: early benefits of practice seem to cease"@en, "Der Buckel: frühe Erträge der Praxis scheinen zu versiegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A stage where the first gains from meditation, pathworking or disciplines seem to end and one is urged to abandon practice; it must be passed through, as in any learning involving life change."@en ;
    skos:note "Not counted as a condition of failure: the cessation of early benefits is named and read as a hump to be passed through, not as a sign that the practice failed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 180; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMacroMicroInitiations a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Macroscopic and microscopic initiations"@en, "Makroskopische und mikroskopische Initiationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Macroscopic initiations are global life shocks (relationship collapse, business crash, terminal diagnosis); microscopic ones are specific, like a sudden interest in a disliked subject, a small flame (Ace of Wands) that can burn out if ignored."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 180-181; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMicroInitiationCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Micro-initiations burn out if smothered"@en, "Mikro-Initiationen erlöschen, wenn sie erstickt werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's sudden wish to do an accounts course illustrates a new interest that could easily burn out if ignored."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMacroMicroInitiations ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 181; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCThresholdRecognitionKey a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognising the threshold is key to all initiation"@en, "Das Erkennen der Schwelle ist Schlüssel jeder Initiation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognising that one stands at a crossroads or threshold of change is called the key to all initiations; in initiatory periods this recognition is all-important."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCThresholdRecognition ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCTransitionPatternShedding ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 177, 181, 183; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAPIEInitiation a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "APIE formula applied to initiation"@en, "APIE-Formel angewandt auf Initiation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assess, Plan, Implement, Evaluate, Hine's formula reused for thresholds of change."@en ;
    skos:note "The formula is introduced earlier in the book, in chapter 5 Playing with Chaos, outside this section; here it is applied again to thresholds of change."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 181; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAPIEAssess a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Assess"@en, "Einschätzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stop and assess your situation, examining all possible future actions (there are more than first appear), gathering information by option lists, divination, dream oracles or consulting a deity; often you need only make yourself vulnerable to Change."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 181; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAPIEPlan a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Plan"@en, "Planen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having chosen a course, plan what you need: material, magical, financial resources and especially others' support; be ready to carry it on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 181; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAPIEImplement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Implement"@en, "Umsetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do what must be done, examining your motives for not continuing when fear intervenes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 181; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInertiaFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unacknowledged fear appears as inertia and laziness"@en, "Unerkannte Angst zeigt sich als Trägheit und Faulheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "At implementation fear often intervenes; unadmitted fears show up as inertia and laziness."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: inertia and laziness at the stage of implementation mark unacknowledged fear. No deadline; the failure is put on the operator. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAPIEImplement."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 181-182; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBarrierBreachedSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Each breached barrier releases pleasure and momentum"@en, "Jede überwundene Schranke setzt Lust und Schwung frei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each step forward gives momentum to the next, and each barrier broken releases a surge of pleasure and freedom."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: each step forward gives momentum to the next and each barrier passed releases a surge of pleasure and freedom. Felt from within; no deadline. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAPIEImplement."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAPIEEvaluate a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Evaluate"@en, "Auswerten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assimilate: beyond writing the magical record, look back over the initiatory period, see what happened and how you handled it and what you learned, making knowledge flesh until it seems natural."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFearBodilyGnosis a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear as the bodily gnosis that resists change"@en, "Angst als Körpergnosis, die Wandel abwehrt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Initiatory states bring fear, especially when macro-initiations make coping strategies useless; fear is an excitatory fight/flight state reinforcing patterns that hold change at bay."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFearIntoExcitementYieldsMomentum a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Fear turned into excitement gives momentum over a threshold"@en, "In Erregung verwandelte Angst gibt Schwung über eine Schwelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fear deconstructed into excitement by Emotional Engineering can be used to gather momentum into change instead of reinforcing resistance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFearIntoExcitement ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCThresholdMomentum ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCFearIntoExcitement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Deconstructing fear into excitement"@en, "Angst in Erregung umwandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Apply Emotional Engineering to fear so it becomes excitement used to gather momentum across a threshold instead of reinforcing resistance."@en ;
    skos:note "Applies pmp:ChaosMagicCondCEmotionalEngineering from chapter 9 to fear."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCThresholdMomentum a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Momentum to cross a threshold of change"@en, "Schwung zum Überschreiten einer Wandlungsschwelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Excitement used as fuel for moving into change."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 182; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRelaxIntoFear a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Relax into Fear"@en, "In die Angst hinein entspannen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Orient yourself to be open to every possibility of each moment in receptive wonder, knowing any event may spin you into Illumination; let arousal be a strength; in initiatory confusion free yourself from past and anticipated futures and live in bodily presence; turn fear into wonder and into fuel to examine thresholds and personal demons."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 182-183; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPanNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pan"@en, "Pan"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Great God Pan embodies the suddenness of illumination and creative derangement, the passage from everyday perception to divine inspiration, able to pounce anywhere with the insight that all things live and matter."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Pan", "the Great God Pan" ;
    pm:nameRole "god of creative derangement and sudden illumination" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 182-183; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRelaxIntoFearYieldsOpenness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxing into fear lets wild magic in"@en, "Entspannung in die Angst lässt wilde Magie herein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allowing oneself to be vulnerable to change is said to let wild magic and the force of surprise into one's life."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRelaxIntoFear ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCWildMagicOpenness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 182-183; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCWildMagicOpenness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Openness to wild magic and sudden illumination"@en, "Offenheit für wilde Magie und plötzliche Erleuchtung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Vulnerability to change lets wild magic and surprise into life; the state counts as a kind of ecstasy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 183; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSahaja a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sahaja: spontaneity in initiatory periods"@en, "Sahaja: Spontaneität in Initiationsphasen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one relaxes within initiatory periods, dropping set routines and learned responses, one can act with greater freedom; such periods are windows for major work on oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 183; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCAchievableRealityThreshold a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold-shifting techniques in initiatory periods (NLP, Vivation, Bioenergetics)"@en, "Schwellenverschiebende Techniken in Initiationsphasen (NLP, Vivation, Bioenergetik)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use anything that shifts your Achievable Reality threshold, e.g. procedures from NLP, Vivation, Bioenergetics or psychotherapies, during initiatory windows."@en ;
    skos:note "Techniques named but not described."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 183; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSurrenderOfControl a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Hard to induce initiatory states; control must be surrendered"@en, "Initiationszustände kaum herbeiführbar; Kontrolle muss abgegeben werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is difficult to propel oneself deliberately into initiatory states, especially since at some point one must surrender control."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSahaja ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 183; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAddictionToSameness a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Addiction to sameness: habit in place of observation in a crisis"@en, "Sucht nach Gleichförmigkeit: Gewohnheit statt Beobachtung in der Krise"@de ;
    skos:definition "The initiatory crisis shows how fragile everyday experience is; being used to sameness, people cope badly with novelty and in a crisis fall back on learned habits instead of observing what is happening, while the magician must reckon with an abyss round any corner and meet head-on whatever rushes at him."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiationAsProcess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 183-184; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiatoryCycles a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognising one's own initiatory cycles"@en, "Erkennen der eigenen Initiationszyklen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In time you come to recognise your own cycles of peaks, troughs and plateaus, foresee an initiatory period and brace for it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 183-184; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDismemberment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Descent into the underworld and dismemberment"@en, "Abstieg in die Unterwelt und Zerstückelung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Myths of underworld descent and rites of passage; shamanic death by dismemberment and remaking with an extra part; voluntary as meditation in Tibetan Chod, involuntary elsewhere; in Western magic both willed and seemingly spontaneous within a belief system."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 184; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCHineDismemberment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hine's dismemberment experiences"@en, "Hines Zerstückelungserfahrungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine reports being burnt alive on the pyre of Kali and losing an eye torn out by the Morrigan."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 184; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMorriganNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Morrigan"@en, "Die Morrigan"@de ;
    skos:definition "Named as having torn out Hine's eye in an initiatory confrontation."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "the Morrigan" ;
    pm:nameRole "initiating goddess in an underworld ordeal" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 184; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCUnderworldDescentNecessary a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Periodic underworld descents are necessary"@en, "Periodische Unterweltabstiege sind notwendig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recurring underworld descents are called a required phase of personal development's cycle."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDismemberment ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiationAsProcess ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 184; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDwellerOnTheThreshold a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Dweller on the Threshold"@en, "Der Hüter der Schwelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the Western Esoteric Tradition a key initiatory encounter; Hine reads it as grasping the gap between the fiction the ego keeps of itself and what we truly are."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "The Dweller on the Threshold" ;
    pm:nameRole "initiatory confrontation figure" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 184; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSeeingYourself a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking responsibility for all of oneself"@en, "Verantwortung für das ganze Selbst übernehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Letting light into the hidden corners of the self and owning one's shortcomings, blind spots and weaknesses, above all those one is loath to admit; the text calls the core of this ordeal the beginning of seeing oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 184-185; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSeeingYourselfNecessary a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking responsibility for all of oneself before the journey proceeds"@en, "Verantwortung für das ganze Selbst, bevor die Reise weitergeht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accepting light into one's dark corners and responsibility for shortcomings and blind spots must happen for the initiatory journey to continue; such ordeals have to be worked through."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSeeingYourself ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInitiationAsProcess ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Ordeals not worked through come back to haunt one until they are tackled and grow into obsessional complexes, demons with power over one; people may stay stuck there for years." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 184-185; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCUnworkedOrdealsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unworked ordeals become obsessional complexes"@en, "Unbearbeitete Prüfungen werden zu obsessiven Komplexen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordeals not worked through return to haunt until tackled and grow into demons with power over us; many stay stuck here for years or keep returning to it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: ordeals not worked through come back and grow into obsessional complexes; people may stay stuck there for years or keep returning to it. No deadline, though a duration of years is named; the failure is put on the operator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 185; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCShamanicOrdeals a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic physical ordeals"@en, "Schamanische körperliche Prüfungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Isolation from the tribe reinforced by fasting, going without sleep, and exposure to heat or cold."@en ;
    skos:note "Reported of shamanic cultures, not prescribed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 185; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCOrdealsYieldAlteredStates a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Physical ordeals produce altered states"@en, "Körperliche Prüfungen erzeugen veränderte Zustände"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fasting, going without sleep and exposure to heat or cold are called powerful means of bringing about altered states of consciousness."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCShamanicOrdeals ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAlteredStates ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 185; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAlteredStates a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Altered states of consciousness"@en, "Veränderte Bewusstseinszustände"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordeals are said to be strong means of inducing altered states."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 185; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAutosymbolicImages a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Descent into the Deep Mind and autosymbolic allies"@en, "Abstieg in den Tiefengeist und autosymbolische Verbündete"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like a snake sloughing skin, one sheds outdated patterns; descending into the Deep Mind one relies on intuition; with Social and Personal worlds dismantled the Mythic World dominates and the Deep Mind speaks in autosymbolic images, entities that may become allies or guides, often after testing the initiate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 185-186; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMisguides a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Misguides: spirits who flatter you as uniquely illuminated"@en, "Irreführer: Geister, die einem einzigartige Erleuchtung schmeicheln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not every spirit met in the underworld is helpful or benign; some mislead, and one must rely on truthsense or discrimination, as an elder brother once warned Hine against spirits that announce a false dawn at the dark moon. The misguides to watch for most tell you that you are illuminated beyond anyone else; they are pieces of the ego trying to save itself and seek to seduce you into feeding your complexes."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCAutosymbolicImages ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 185-186; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCOvercomingMisguides a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Overcoming misguide spirits by recognition"@en, "Überwindung von Irreführern durch Erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Overcome misleading spirits not by astral combat but by recognising they hold no power over you and that you see through their seductions; shed light on as many buried complexes as possible."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 186; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCUnderworldAllies a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Allies, secret routes and places of power in the underworld"@en, "Verbündete, geheime Wege und Kraftorte in der Unterwelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Passing the guides' tests yields allies who can be called on after returning, secret routes and places of power accessible later; spirits test strength and dislike those who will not take chances."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 186; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCSpiritNamesForMasks a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Learning spirit names in the underworld to place in masks"@en, "Erlernen von Geisternamen in der Unterwelt zur Einbindung in Masken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some Amerind shamanic traditions descend periodically to learn spirit names, which are brought back and placed in masks or ritual objects."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 186; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCUnderworldMapping a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Underworld mapping"@en, "Kartierung der Unterwelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A benefit of the ordeal stage is gaining or checking a symbolic map of the linked worlds (e.g. the Tree of Life); one can metaprogram the Deep Mind to accept different maps, images arising accordingly; such maps likely derive from early shamans' ordeals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 186-187; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIllumination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Illumination as peak of initiation via death/rebirth"@en, "Erleuchtung als Höhepunkt der Initiation durch Tod/Wiedergeburt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The peak of initiation is death/rebirth and illumination, common to mystery religions, magical systems and secular movements, suggesting an essential mode of psychic change; reached by many psycho-technologies, LSD, or spontaneously."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 187; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIlluminationMarksSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Eight marks of an illumination experience"@en, "Acht Merkmale eines Erleuchtungserlebnisses"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unity and fading of self-other divide; transcendence of space-time; positive sensations; sense of the numinous; certitude of its reality; paradoxical insights; transience; resulting change in attitude and behaviour."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: eight marks of illumination: unity, transcendence of space and time, positive sensations, the numinous, certitude, paradoxical insight, transience, and a resulting change in attitude and behaviour. No deadline; only the last is observable by others. It concerns pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIllumination."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 187; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIlluminationNeurology a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Neurological account of illumination"@en, "Neurologische Erklärung der Erleuchtung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Illumination is said to be a global reorganisation of brain activity: loss of ego boundary implicating the reticular formation, floating sensation implicating the limbic system processing proprioception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 187-188; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDissipativeStructuresStages a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five-stage transformation model (after Prigogine)"@en, "Fünfstufiges Wandlungsmodell (nach Prigogine)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using Prigogine's dissipative structures, Hine sets out core stages: change, crisis, transcendence, transformation, predisposition to further change; applicable to neurological evolution through psycho-technology."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Condensed Chaos, after Ilya Prigogine's theory of dissipative structures" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 188; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBornAgain a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Light visions and being born again"@en, "Lichtvisionen und Wiedergeburt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visions of light (shamans, St Paul, acid trippers) and the old self dying for a new one are widespread; cultures with a single mythic reality understand it, shamanic cultures take it literally."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 188-189; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCDeathRebirthDisturbing a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Death-rebirth is disturbing without a cultural frame"@en, "Tod-Wiedergeburt verstört ohne kulturellen Rahmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For many the experience unsettles and disturbs when no dominant cultural backdrop exists to explain it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIllumination ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 189; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmp:ChaosMagicCondCLSDDeathRebirth a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "LSD death-rebirth under controlled conditions"@en, "LSD-Tod-Wiedergeburt unter kontrollierten Bedingungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "LSD as a route to death-rebirth experience; Huxley, Leary and Grof stressed controlled conditions rather than indiscriminate use."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 189; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPsychoactiveValidity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the view that drug-induced experiences are less valid"@en, "Gegen die Ansicht, drogeninduzierte Erfahrungen seien weniger gültig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine rejects western spiritual authorities who rank drug-triggered experience below that from spiritual practice, citing the role of psychoactives in shamanic training and Huxley, Leary and Grof on LSD's benefits."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the western authorities he opposes are unnamed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 189; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPsychoactiveSetCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Psychoactive effects depend on set and culture; use controlled conditions"@en, "Psychoaktive Wirkung hängt von Einstellung und Kultur ab; kontrollierte Bedingungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "LSD's effects depend heavily on beliefs, expectations and conditioning; it should be used under controlled conditions, not indiscriminately."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondCLSDDeathRebirth ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 189; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCBeliefWallFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Acid experience can wall one off from further change"@en, "Säureerfahrung kann gegen weiteren Wandel abschotten"@de ;
    skos:definition "LSD may bring lasting positive change or uncritical acceptance of a belief set that blocks further transformation, as with burnt-out acidheads turned born-again evangelicals; assimilation, not the experience, decides."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: an LSD experience that ends in uncritical adoption of a closed set of beliefs, walling the person off from further change, as with acidheads turned born-again evangelicals. No deadline; the failure is put on the person's assimilation and cultural expectations rather than on the substance. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicCondCLSDDeathRebirth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 189; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCZeroStates a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Resting on \"I'm illuminated now\""@en, "Ausruhen auf „Ich bin jetzt erleuchtet“"@de ;
    skos:definition "Westerners are not granted a shaman's role after illumination; it is tempting to sit on one's laurels, but what one does afterwards is critical; the zero state of having arrived is seductive; transformation is paid for with eternal vigilance."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIllumination ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, pp. 189-190; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCConditioningReturnsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conditioning creeps back after illumination"@en, "Konditionierung kriecht nach der Erleuchtung zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conditioning patterns are insidious and creep back while attention is elsewhere, lulling one back into patterns thought overcome; illumination is a peak, not the end point."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: conditioned patterns creep back after illumination when vigilance lapses. No deadline; the failure is put on the operator. It concerns pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIllumination."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 190; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPeriodicDeathRebirth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Repeated death-rebirth experiences needed in the West"@en, "Im Westen sind viele periodische Tod-Wiedergeburt-Erfahrungen nötig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those in the Western initiation cycle tend to need many death-rebirth experiences, each reshuffling parts of the psyche."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 190; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCHolotropicPerspective a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lasting benefits of death-rebirth"@en, "Dauerhafte Wirkungen der Tod-Wiedergeburt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Death-rebirth can bring lasting relief of emotional, interpersonal and psychosomatic troubles which resisted orthodox treatment, and, as Hine postulates, is an adaptive learning that widens perspective toward a holotropic view in which new insights into self and universe and new concepts can be manifested."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 190; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCGnosisTwoLevels a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gnosis on two levels"@en, "Gnosis auf zwei Ebenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gnosis is the peak of no-mind, one-pointed focus or samadhi at the height of any magical trance, and Knowledge of the Heart, hard to verbalise but sharable only through experience, an understanding that compels action; as you work magic, magic works on you."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), ch. 10 Are You Illuminated?, p. 190; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .


#
# For Further Information: The Magical Pact of the Illuminates of Thanateros
#

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIOTGrades a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "IOT (The Pact): grades, Temples and Study Groups"@en, "IOT (Der Pakt): Grade, Tempel und Studiengruppen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Illuminates of Thanateros (IOT), called the Pact, founded by Peter J. Carroll in the 1980s, follows only the meta-approach of Chaos Magic, emphasises technical competence from personal and group experience, and is structured by a hierarchy of grades reflecting skill, commitment and organisational responsibility, organised in Temples and Study Groups."@en ;
    skos:note "The date is that of the notice in this book; the Pact itself is said to have been inaugurated in the 1980s."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "The Magical Pact of the Illuminates of Thanateros, founded in the 1980s on the writings of Peter J. Carroll" ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Condensed Chaos: An Introduction to Chaos Magic (Tempe: New Falcon, 1995, first edition, second printing 1996), notice For Further Information, The Magical Pact of the Illuminates of Thanateros, p. 191; read in a full-text layer of the second printing" .

pmc:ChaosMagicCondCNMPBeforeInitiation a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Novice/Mentor Program precedes IOT initiation"@en, "Novizen-/Mentorenprogramm geht der IOT-Initiation voraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The NMP, a postal course in elementary Chaos magic technique with an assigned Mentor assessing progress, comes before initiation into the IOT."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCNoviceMentorProgram ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIOTGrades ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:CondensedChaos ;
